      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "mt1",
      "content": [
        "Acts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "1",
      "sid": "ACT 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Prologue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LUK 1:1-4",
          "content": [
            "Luke 1:1–4"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 1:1"
        },
        "In my first book, O Theophilus, I wrote about all that Jesus began to do and to teach, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 1:2"
        },
        "until the day He was taken up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to heaven"
          ]
        },
        ", after giving instructions through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit to the apostles He had chosen. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 1:3"
        },
        "After His suffering, He presented Himself to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " with many convincing proofs ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " He was alive. He appeared to them over ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a span "
          ]
        },
        " of forty days and spoke about the kingdom of God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 1:4"
        },
        "And while they were gathered together,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "eating together"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " He commanded them: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Do not leave Jerusalem, but wait for the ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "gift"
              ]
            },
            " the Father promised, which you have heard Me ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "discuss "
              ]
            },
            ". ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "5",
              "sid": "ACT 1:5"
            },
            "For John baptized with water, but in a few days you will be baptized with ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Holy Spirit.",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "1:5 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "For John baptized in water, but in a few days you will be baptized in the Holy Spirit"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "; cited in ",
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "ACT 11:16",
                      "content": [
                        "Acts 11:16"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Ascension"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "MRK 16:19-20",
          "content": [
            "Mark 16:19–20"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LUK 24:50-53",
          "content": [
            "Luke 24:50–53"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 1:6"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they came together, they asked Him, “Lord, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will You"
          ]
        },
        " at this time restore the kingdom to Israel?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 1:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " replied, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“It is not for you to know times or seasons that the Father has fixed by His own authority. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "8",
              "sid": "ACT 1:8"
            },
            "But you will receive power ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "when"
              ]
            },
            " the Holy Spirit comes upon you, and you will be My witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " ends of the earth.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 1:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " He had said this, they watched as He was taken up, and a cloud hid Him from their sight. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 1:10"
        },
        "They were looking intently into the sky as He was going, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " suddenly two men dressed in white stood beside them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 1:11"
        },
        "“Men of Galilee,” they said, “why do you stand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "here"
          ]
        },
        " looking into the sky? This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "same"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus, who has been taken from you into heaven, will come back in the same way you have seen Him go into heaven.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Matthias Replaces Judas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 1:12"
        },
        "Then they returned to Jerusalem from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Mount of Olives, which is near ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the city"
          ]
        },
        ", a Sabbath day’s journey away.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "A Sabbath day’s journey "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "is 2,000 cubits (approximately 3,000 feet or 914.4 meters)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 1:13"
        },
        "When they arrived, they went to the upper room where they were staying: Peter and John, James and Andrew, Philip and Thomas, Bartholomew and Matthew, James ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "son"
          ]
        },
        " of Alphaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "son"
          ]
        },
        " of James. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 1:14"
        },
        "With one accord they all continued in prayer, along with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " women and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with His brothers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 1:15"
        },
        "In those days Peter stood up among the brothers (a gathering of about a hundred ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " twenty) ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 1:16"
        },
        "“Brothers, the Scripture had to be fulfilled that the Holy Spirit foretold through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " mouth of David concerning Judas, who became a guide for those who arrested Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 1:17"
        },
        "He was one of our number and shared in this ministry.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 1:18"
        },
        "(Now with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " reward for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " wickedness ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Judas"
          ]
        },
        " bought a field; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " he fell headlong and burst open in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " middle, and all his intestines spilled out. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 1:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This"
          ]
        },
        " became known to all who lived in Jerusalem, so they called that field in their own language Akeldama, that is, Field of Blood.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 1:20"
        },
        "“For it is written in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " book of Psalms:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "May"
          ]
        },
        " his place be deserted;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "let there be no ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " to dwell in it,’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 69:25",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 69:25"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "and,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "May"
          ]
        },
        " another take his position.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 109:8",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 109:8"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 1:21"
        },
        "Therefore it is necessary ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to choose"
          ]
        },
        " one of the men who have accompanied us ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " whole time the Lord Jesus went in and out among us, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 1:22"
        },
        "beginning from John’s baptism until the day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " was taken up from us. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "For"
          ]
        },
        " one of these must become a witness with us of His resurrection.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 1:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they proposed two ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        ": Joseph called Barsabbas (",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "also"
          ]
        },
        " known as Justus) and Matthias. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 1:24"
        },
        "And they prayed, “Lord, You know everyone’s heart. Show ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        " which of these two You have chosen ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 1:25"
        },
        "to take up this ministry and apostleship, which Judas abandoned to go to his ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "rightful"
          ]
        },
        " place.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 1:26"
        },
        "Then they cast lots, and the lot fell to Matthias. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " he was added to the eleven apostles."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "2",
      "sid": "ACT 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Holy Spirit at Pentecost"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GEN 11:1-9",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 11:1–9"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 23:15-22",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 23:15–22"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 2:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the day of Pentecost",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Harvest"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "(see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 23:16",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 23:16"
                  ]
                },
                ") or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Weeks"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "(see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 34:22",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 34:22"
                  ]
                },
                ")."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " came, they were all together in one ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "place"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 2:2"
        },
        "Suddenly a sound like a mighty rushing wind came from heaven and filled the whole house where they were sitting. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 2:3"
        },
        "They saw tongues like flames of fire that separated and came to rest on each of them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 2:4"
        },
        "And they ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " all filled with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit and began to speak in other tongues as the Spirit enabled them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 2:5"
        },
        "Now there were dwelling",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "staying"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; similarly in verse 14"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " in Jerusalem God-fearing Jews from every nation under heaven. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 2:6"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " this sound rang out, a crowd came together in bewilderment, because each one heard them speaking ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " own language."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 2:7"
        },
        "Astounded and amazed, they asked, “Are not all these who are speaking Galileans? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 2:8"
        },
        "How is it then that each of us hears ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in his own native language? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 2:9"
        },
        "Parthians, Medes, and Elamites; residents of Mesopotamia, Judea and Cappadocia, Pontus and Asia,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:9 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, the Roman Province of Asia, located in what is now western Turkey"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 2:10"
        },
        "Phrygia and Pamphylia, Egypt and the parts of Libya near Cyrene; visitors from Rome, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 2:11"
        },
        "both Jews and converts to Judaism; Cretans and Arabs— we hear them declaring the wonders of God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in"
          ]
        },
        " our own tongues!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 2:12"
        },
        "Astounded and perplexed, they asked one another, “What does this mean?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 2:13"
        },
        "But others mocked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “They are drunk on new wine!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter Addresses the Crowd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 16:1-11",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 16:1–11"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JOL 2:28-32",
          "content": [
            "Joel 2:28–32"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 2:14"
        },
        "Then Peter stood up with the Eleven, lifted up his voice, and addressed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the crowd"
          ]
        },
        ": “Men of Judea and all who dwell in Jerusalem, let this be known to you, and listen carefully to my words. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 2:15"
        },
        "These ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        " are not drunk, as you suppose. It is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "only the"
          ]
        },
        " third hour of the day!",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, nine in the morning"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 2:16"
        },
        "No, this is what was spoken by the prophet Joel:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 2:17"
        },
        "‘In the last days, God says,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I will pour out My Spirit on all people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Your sons and daughters will prophesy,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "your young men will see visions,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "your old men will dream dreams."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 2:18"
        },
        "Even on My menservants and maidservants"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I will pour out My Spirit in those days,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and they will prophesy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 2:19"
        },
        "I will show wonders in the heavens above"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and signs on the earth below,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "blood and fire and billows of smoke."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 2:20"
        },
        "The sun will be turned to darkness,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the moon to blood,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "before the coming ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the"
          ]
        },
        " great and glorious Day of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 2:21"
        },
        "And everyone who calls on the name of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "will be saved.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "JOL 2:28-32",
                  "content": [
                    "Joel 2:28–32"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 2:22"
        },
        "Men of Israel, listen to this message: Jesus of Nazareth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " a man certified by God to you by miracles, wonders, and signs, which God did among you through Him, as you yourselves know. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 2:23"
        },
        "He was delivered up by God’s set plan and foreknowledge, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and you"
          ]
        },
        ", by the hands of the lawless, put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " to death by nailing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " to the cross. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 2:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " God raised Him from the dead, releasing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " from the agony of death, because it was impossible ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for death"
          ]
        },
        " to keep Him in its ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "grip"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 2:25"
        },
        "David says about Him:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘I saw",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "I foresaw"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see verse 31."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " the Lord always before me;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "because He is at my right hand, I will not be shaken."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 2:26"
        },
        "Therefore my heart is glad and my tongue rejoices;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "my body also will dwell in hope,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 2:27"
        },
        "because You will not abandon my soul to Hades,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "nor will You let Your Holy One see decay."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 2:28"
        },
        "You have made known to me ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " paths of life;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "You will fill me with joy in Your presence.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 16:8-11",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 16:8–11"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 2:29"
        },
        "Brothers, I can tell you with confidence that the patriarch David died and was buried, and his tomb is with us to this day. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 2:30"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " he was a prophet and knew that God had promised him on oath that He would place ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his descendants"
          ]
        },
        " on his throne.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:30 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "on oath that He would place out of the fruit of his loins on his throne"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "on oath out of the fruit of his loins, according to the flesh, to raise up Christ to sit on his throne"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 132:11",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 132:11"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 2:31"
        },
        "Foreseeing this, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "David"
          ]
        },
        " spoke about the resurrection of the Christ, that He was not abandoned to Hades, nor ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " His body see decay. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 2:32"
        },
        "God has raised this Jesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to life"
          ]
        },
        ", to which we are all witnesses."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 2:33"
        },
        "Exalted, then, to the right hand of God, He has received from the Father the promised Holy Spirit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " has poured out what you now see and hear. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 2:34"
        },
        "For David ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " not ascend into heaven, but he himself says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘The Lord said to my Lord,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "“Sit at My right hand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 2:35"
        },
        "until I make Your enemies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "a footstool for Your feet.”’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:35 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 110:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 110:1"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 2:36"
        },
        "Therefore ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " all Israel know with certainty that God has made this Jesus, whom you crucified, both Lord and Christ!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Three Thousand Believe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 2:37"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they were cut to the heart and asked Peter and the other apostles, “Brothers, what shall we do?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 2:38"
        },
        "Peter replied, “Repent and be baptized, every one of you, in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of your sins, and you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 2:39"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This"
          ]
        },
        " promise belongs to you and your children and to all who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " far off — to all whom ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord our God will call to Himself.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 2:40"
        },
        "With many other words he testified, and he urged them, “Be saved from this corrupt generation.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 2:41"
        },
        "Those who embraced his message were baptized, and about three thousand were added  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to the believers "
          ]
        },
        " that day.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:41 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "about three thousand souls were added that day"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Fellowship of Believers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 4:32-37",
          "content": [
            "Acts 4:32–37"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "ACT 2:42"
        },
        "They devoted themselves to the apostles’ teaching and to the fellowship, to the breaking of bread and to prayer. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "ACT 2:43"
        },
        "A sense of awe",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:43 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "fear"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " came over everyone, and the apostles performed many wonders and signs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "ACT 2:44"
        },
        "All the believers were together and had everything in common. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "ACT 2:45"
        },
        "Selling ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " possessions and goods, they shared with anyone who was in need."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "ACT 2:46"
        },
        "With one accord they continued ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to meet"
          ]
        },
        " daily in the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:46 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the temple"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and to break bread from house ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to house"
          ]
        },
        ", sharing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " meals with gladness and sincerity of heart, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "ACT 2:47"
        },
        "praising God and enjoying ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " favor of all the people. And the Lord added to their number daily those who were being saved."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "3",
      "sid": "ACT 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Lame Man Walks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 3:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One afternoon "
          ]
        },
        " Peter and John were going up to the temple at the hour of prayer, the ninth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "hour"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, three in the afternoon"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 3:2"
        },
        "And a man who was lame from birth was being carried ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to"
          ]
        },
        " the temple gate called Beautiful, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " he was put every day to beg from those entering the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the temple"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 8"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 3:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " he saw Peter and John about to enter, he asked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " for money."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 3:4"
        },
        "Peter looked directly at him, as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " John. “Look at us!” said ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 3:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " gave them his attention, expecting to receive something from them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 3:6"
        },
        "But Peter said, “Silver ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " gold I do not have, but what I have I give you: In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, get up and walk!",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "SBL, NE, and WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, walk!"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 3:7"
        },
        "Taking him by the right hand, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " helped him up, and at once ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man’s"
          ]
        },
        " feet and ankles were made strong. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 3:8"
        },
        "He sprang to his feet and began to walk. Then he went with them into the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        ", walking and leaping and praising God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 3:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " all the people saw him walking and praising God, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 3:10"
        },
        "they recognized him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " who used to sit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "begging"
          ]
        },
        " at the Beautiful Gate of the temple, and they were filled with wonder and amazement at what had happened to him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter Speaks in Solomon’s Colonnade"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 18:15-22",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 18:15–22"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 3:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " clung to Peter and John, all the people were astonished ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ran to them in the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "walkway"
          ]
        },
        " called Solomon’s Colonnade.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in the colonnade called Solomon’s"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 3:12"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " Peter saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", he addressed the people: “Men of Israel, why are you surprised by this? Why do you stare at us as if by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " own power or godliness ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we"
          ]
        },
        " had made ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this man"
          ]
        },
        " walk?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 3:13"
        },
        "The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our fathers, has glorified His servant",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "His child"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 26"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Jesus. You handed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him over"
          ]
        },
        " and rejected ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " before Pilate, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "even though"
          ]
        },
        " he had decided to release ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 3:14"
        },
        "You rejected the Holy and Righteous One and asked that a murderer be released to you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 3:15"
        },
        "You killed the Author of life, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " God raised ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " we are witnesses of this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "fact"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 3:16"
        },
        "By faith in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " name of Jesus, this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " whom you see and know has been made strong. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is Jesus’"
          ]
        },
        " name and the faith that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "comes"
          ]
        },
        " through Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " has given him this complete healing in your presence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 3:17"
        },
        "And now, brothers, I know that you acted in ignorance, as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " your leaders. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 3:18"
        },
        "But in this way ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " has fulfilled what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " foretold through all the prophets, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "saying that"
          ]
        },
        " His Christ would suffer. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 3:19"
        },
        "Repent, then, and turn back, so that your sins may be wiped away, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 3:20"
        },
        "that times of refreshing may come from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " presence of the Lord, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " He may send Jesus, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Christ, who has been appointed for you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 3:21"
        },
        "Heaven must take Him in until ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "comes"
          ]
        },
        " for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " restoration of all things, which God announced long ago through His holy prophets. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 3:22"
        },
        "For Moses said, ‘The Lord your God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers. You must listen to Him in everything He tells you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 18:15",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 18:15"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 3:23"
        },
        "Everyone who does not listen  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to Him "
          ]
        },
        " will be completely cut off from among ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " people.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 18:19",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 18:19"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 3:24"
        },
        "Indeed, all the prophets from Samuel on, as many as have spoken, have proclaimed these days. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 3:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And"
          ]
        },
        " you are sons of the prophets and of the covenant God made with your fathers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " He said to Abraham, ‘Through your offspring all the families of the earth will be blessed.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 22:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 22:18"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 3:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " God raised up His Servant, He sent Him first to you to bless you by turning each ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of you"
          ]
        },
        " from your wicked ways.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "4",
      "sid": "ACT 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter and John before the Sanhedrin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 4:1"
        },
        "While ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter and John"
          ]
        },
        " were speaking to the people, the priests and the captain of the temple guard and the Sadducees came up to them, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 4:2"
        },
        "greatly disturbed that they were teaching the people and proclaiming in Jesus the resurrection of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 4:3"
        },
        "They seized ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter and John"
          ]
        },
        ", and because it was evening, they put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in custody until the next day. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 4:4"
        },
        "But many who heard the message believed, and the number of men grew to about five thousand."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 4:5"
        },
        "The next day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " rulers, elders, and scribes assembled in Jerusalem, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 4:6"
        },
        "along with Annas the high priest, Caiaphas, John, Alexander, and many others from the high priest’s family. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 4:7"
        },
        "They had ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter and John"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "brought"
          ]
        },
        " in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began to question them: “By what power or what name ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " you do this?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 4:8"
        },
        "Then Peter, filled with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit, said to them, “Rulers and elders of the people! ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 4:9"
        },
        "If we are being examined today about a kind service ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to a"
          ]
        },
        " man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who was"
          ]
        },
        " lame, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to determine"
          ]
        },
        " how he was healed, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 4:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "then"
          ]
        },
        " let this be known to all of you and to all the people of Israel: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " by the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom you crucified ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " whom God raised from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " stands before you healed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 4:11"
        },
        "This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " is"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘the stone you builders rejected,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "which has become ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " cornerstone.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 118:22",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 118:22"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 4:12"
        },
        "Salvation exists in no one else, for there is no other name under heaven given to men by which we must be saved.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Name Forbidden"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 4:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they saw the boldness of Peter and John and realized that they were unschooled, ordinary men, they marveled and took note that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these men"
          ]
        },
        " had been with Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 4:14"
        },
        "And seeing the man who had been healed standing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " with them, they had nothing to say in response. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 4:15"
        },
        "So they ordered them to leave the Sanhedrin",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Council"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " then conferred together."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 4:16"
        },
        "“What shall we do with these men?” they asked. “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It"
          ]
        },
        " is clear to everyone living ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in"
          ]
        },
        " Jerusalem that a remarkable miracle has occurred through them, and we cannot deny ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 4:17"
        },
        "But to keep ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this message"
          ]
        },
        " from spreading any further among the people, we must warn them not to speak to anyone in this name.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 4:18"
        },
        "Then they called them in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "again"
          ]
        },
        " and commanded ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " not to speak ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " teach at all in the name of Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 4:19"
        },
        "But Peter and John replied, “Judge for yourselves whether it is right in God’s sight to listen to you rather than God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 4:20"
        },
        "For we cannot stop speaking about what we have seen and heard.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 4:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " further threats they let them go. They could not find a way to punish them, because ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "all"
          ]
        },
        " the people were glorifying God for what had happened. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 4:22"
        },
        "For the man who was miraculously healed was over forty years ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "old"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Believers’ Prayer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 2:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 2:1–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 4:23"
        },
        "On their release, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter and John"
          ]
        },
        " returned to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " own people and reported everything that the chief priests and elders had said to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 4:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the believers"
          ]
        },
        " heard this, they lifted up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " voices to God with one accord. “Sovereign Lord,” they said, “You made the heaven and the earth and the sea and everything in them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 4:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You"
          ]
        },
        " spoke by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " mouth of Your servant,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "child"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verses 27 and 30"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " our father David:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘Why ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " the nations rage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " peoples plot in vain?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 4:26"
        },
        "The kings of the earth take ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " stand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the rulers gather together"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "against the Lord"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and against His Anointed One.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:26 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "His Christ "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "His Messiah"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 2:1-2",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 2:1–2"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 4:27"
        },
        "In fact, this is the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "very"
          ]
        },
        " city ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " Herod and Pontius Pilate conspired with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Gentiles and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " people of Israel against Your holy servant Jesus, whom You anointed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 4:28"
        },
        "They carried out what Your hand and will had decided beforehand would happen. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 4:29"
        },
        "And now, Lord, consider their threats, and enable Your servants to speak Your word with complete boldness, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 4:30"
        },
        "as You stretch out Your hand to heal and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "perform"
          ]
        },
        " signs and wonders through the name of Your holy servant Jesus.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 4:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " they had prayed, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " meeting place was shaken, and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and spoke the word of God boldly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Sharing among Believers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 2:42-47",
          "content": [
            "Acts 2:42–47"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 4:32"
        },
        "The multitude of believers was one ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in"
          ]
        },
        " heart and soul. No one claimed that any of his possessions was his own, but they shared everything they owned. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 4:33"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "With"
          ]
        },
        " great power the apostles continued to give ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " testimony about the resurrection of the Lord Jesus. And abundant grace was upon them all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 4:34"
        },
        "There were no needy ones among them, because those who owned lands or houses would sell  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their property "
          ]
        },
        ", bring the proceeds from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sales, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 4:35"
        },
        "and lay ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " at the apostles’ feet for distribution ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to"
          ]
        },
        " anyone as he had need."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 4:36"
        },
        "Joseph, a Levite from Cyprus, whom the apostles called Barnabas (meaning Son of Encouragement), ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 4:37"
        },
        "sold a field he owned, brought the money, and laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " at the apostles’ feet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "5",
      "sid": "ACT 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Ananias and Sapphira"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 5:1"
        },
        "Now a man named Ananias, together with his wife Sapphira, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "also"
          ]
        },
        " sold a piece of property. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 5:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "With"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " wife’s full knowledge, he kept back ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " of the proceeds ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for himself"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " brought a portion ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " at the apostles’ feet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 5:3"
        },
        "Then Peter said, “Ananias, how is it that Satan has filled your heart to lie to the Holy Spirit and withhold ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " of the proceeds from the land? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 5:4"
        },
        "Did it not belong to you before it was sold? And after it was sold, was it ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "not"
          ]
        },
        " at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " disposal? How could you conceive such a deed in your heart? You have not lied to men, but to God!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 5:5"
        },
        "On hearing these words, Ananias fell down ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " died. And great fear came over all who heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "what had happened"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 5:6"
        },
        "Then the young ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        " stepped forward, wrapped up his ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "body"
          ]
        },
        ", and carried ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " buried ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 5:7"
        },
        "About three hours later his wife also came in, unaware of what had happened. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 5:8"
        },
        "“Tell me,” said Peter, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is this"
          ]
        },
        " the price you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and your husband "
          ]
        },
        " got for the land?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Yes,” she answered, “that is the price.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 5:9"
        },
        "“How could you agree to test the Spirit of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord?” Peter ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "replied"
          ]
        },
        ". “Look, the feet of the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men who"
          ]
        },
        " buried your husband ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " at the door, and they will carry you out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "also"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 5:10"
        },
        "At that instant she fell down at his feet and died. Then the young ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        " came in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        ", finding her dead, carried ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " buried ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " beside her husband. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 5:11"
        },
        "And great fear came over the whole church and all who heard about these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "events"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Apostles Heal Many"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 5:12"
        },
        "The apostles performed many signs and wonders among the people, and with one accord ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the believers gathered together"
          ]
        },
        " in Solomon’s Colonnade. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 5:13"
        },
        "Although the people regarded them highly, no one else dared to join them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 5:14"
        },
        "Yet more and more believers were brought to the Lord — large numbers of both men and women."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 5:15"
        },
        "As a result, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " brought the sick into the streets and laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " on cots and mats, so that at least Peter’s shadow might fall on some of them as he passed by. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 5:16"
        },
        "Crowds also gathered from the towns around Jerusalem, bringing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sick and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those"
          ]
        },
        " tormented by unclean spirits, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of them"
          ]
        },
        " were healed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Apostles Arrested and Freed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 5:17"
        },
        "Then the high priest and all his associates, who belonged to the party of the Sadducees, were filled with jealousy. They went out ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 5:18"
        },
        "and arrested the apostles and put them in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " public jail. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 5:19"
        },
        "But during the night an angel of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord opened the doors of the jail ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " brought them out, saying, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 5:20"
        },
        "“Go, stand in the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the temple"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verses 21, 25, and 42"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " tell the people the full message of this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "new"
          ]
        },
        " life.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 5:21"
        },
        "At daybreak ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the apostles"
          ]
        },
        " entered the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        " as they had been told and began to teach ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the high priest and his associates arrived, they convened the Sanhedrin",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Council"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verses 27, 34, and 41"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "— the full assembly of the elders of Israel— and sent to the jail ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the apostles"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 5:22"
        },
        "But on arriving at the jail, the officers did not find them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they returned with the report: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 5:23"
        },
        "“We found the jail securely locked, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        " the guards posted at the doors; but when we opened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ", we found no one inside.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Apostles before the Sanhedrin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 5:24"
        },
        "When the captain of the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "guard"
          ]
        },
        " and the chief priests heard this account, they were perplexed as to what was happening.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:24 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "as to what this might be"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 5:25"
        },
        "Then someone came in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " announced, “Look, the men you put in jail are standing in the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        " teaching the people!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 5:26"
        },
        "At that point, the captain went with the officers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the apostles"
          ]
        },
        " — ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " not by force, for fear the people would stone ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 5:27"
        },
        "They brought them in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " made ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " stand before the Sanhedrin, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " the high priest interrogated them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 5:28"
        },
        "“We gave you strict orders not to teach in this name,” he said. “Yet you have filled Jerusalem with your teaching and are determined to make us responsible for this man’s blood.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 5:29"
        },
        "But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must obey God rather than men. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 5:30"
        },
        "The God of our fathers raised up Jesus, whom you had killed by hanging ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " on a tree. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 5:31"
        },
        "God exalted Him to His right hand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " Prince and Savior, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in order "
          ]
        },
        " to grant repentance and forgiveness of sins to Israel. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 5:32"
        },
        "We are witnesses of these things, and so ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the Holy Spirit, whom God has given to those who obey Him.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Gamaliel’s Advice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 5:33"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Council members"
          ]
        },
        " heard this, they were enraged, and they resolved",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:33 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "ECM, BYZ, TR, and Tischendorf; or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "they took counsel"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; SBL, NE, and WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "they wanted"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the apostles"
          ]
        },
        " to death. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 5:34"
        },
        "But a Pharisee named Gamaliel, a teacher of the law who was honored by all the people, stood up in the Sanhedrin ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ordered that the men be put outside for a short time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 5:35"
        },
        "“Men of Israel,” he said, “consider carefully what you are about to do to these men. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 5:36"
        },
        "Some time ago Theudas rose up, claiming to be somebody, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " about four hundred men joined ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " was killed, all his followers were dispersed, and it all came to nothing. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 5:37"
        },
        "After ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", Judas the Galilean appeared in the days of the census and drew away people after him. He too perished, and all his followers were scattered."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 5:38"
        },
        "So in the present ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "case"
          ]
        },
        " I advise you: Leave these men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "alone"
          ]
        },
        ". Let them go! For if ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " purpose or endeavor is of human origin, it will fail. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 5:39"
        },
        "But if it is from God, you will not be able to stop them. You may even find yourselves fighting against God.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 5:40"
        },
        "At this, they yielded to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Gamaliel"
          ]
        },
        ". They called the apostles ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in"
          ]
        },
        " and had them flogged. Then they ordered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " not to speak in the name of Jesus, and released ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 5:41"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The apostles"
          ]
        },
        " left the Sanhedrin, rejoicing that they had been counted worthy of suffering disgrace for the Name. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "ACT 5:42"
        },
        "Every day, in the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        " and from house ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to house"
          ]
        },
        ", they did not stop teaching and proclaiming the good news that Jesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the Christ."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "6",
      "sid": "ACT 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Choosing of the Seven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1TI 3:8-13",
          "content": [
            "1 Timothy 3:8–13"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 6:1"
        },
        "In those days ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " the disciples were increasing in number, the Grecian ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jews among them"
          ]
        },
        " began to grumble against the Hebraic ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jews"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Hellenists began to grumble against the Hebrews"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " because their widows were being overlooked in the daily distribution  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of food "
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 6:2"
        },
        "So the Twelve summoned all the disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “It is unacceptable ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " us to neglect the word of God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in order"
          ]
        },
        " to wait on tables. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 6:3"
        },
        "Therefore, brothers, select from among you seven men confirmed to be full of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Spirit and wisdom. We will assign this responsibility ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 6:4"
        },
        "and will devote ourselves to prayer and to the ministry of the word.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 6:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This"
          ]
        },
        " proposal pleased the whole group. They chose Stephen, a man full of faith and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit, as well as Philip, Prochorus, Nicanor, Timon, Parmenas, and Nicolas from Antioch, a convert ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to Judaism"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and Nicolas, a convert of Antioch"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 6:6"
        },
        "They presented ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these seven"
          ]
        },
        " to the apostles,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "—whom they set before the apostles,"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " prayed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " hands on them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 6:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " the word of God continued to spread. The number of disciples in Jerusalem grew rapidly, and a great number of priests became obedient to the faith."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Arrest of Stephen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 6:8"
        },
        "Now Stephen, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who was"
          ]
        },
        " full of grace and power, was performing great wonders and signs among the people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 6:9"
        },
        "But resistance arose from what was called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Synagogue of the Freedmen, including Cyrenians, Alexandrians, and men from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the provinces of"
          ]
        },
        " Cilicia and Asia.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:9 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and those from Cilicia and Asia"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; the Roman Province of Asia was located in what is now western Turkey."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " They disputed with Stephen, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 6:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " they could not stand up to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " wisdom ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " the Spirit by whom he spoke."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 6:11"
        },
        "Then they prompted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " men to say, “We heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Stephen"
          ]
        },
        " speak words of blasphemy against Moses and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "against"
          ]
        },
        " God.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 6:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they stirred up the people, elders, and scribes and confronted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Stephen"
          ]
        },
        ". They seized him and brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " before the Sanhedrin,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Council"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 15"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 6:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " they presented false witnesses ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " said, “This man never stops speaking against this holy place and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "against"
          ]
        },
        " the law. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 6:14"
        },
        "For we have heard him say that Jesus of Nazareth will destroy this place and change the customs that Moses handed down to us.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 6:15"
        },
        "All who were sitting in the Sanhedrin looked intently at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Stephen"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " they saw that his face ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " like ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " face of an angel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "7",
      "sid": "ACT 7"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Stephen’s Address: The Call of Abraham"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GEN 12:1-9",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 12:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 7:1"
        },
        "Then the high priest asked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Stephen"
          ]
        },
        ", “Are these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "charges"
          ]
        },
        " true?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 7:2"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Stephen"
          ]
        },
        " declared: “Brothers and fathers, listen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to me"
          ]
        },
        "! The God of glory appeared to our father Abraham while he was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "still"
          ]
        },
        " in Mesopotamia, before he lived in Haran, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 7:3"
        },
        "and told him, ‘Leave your country and your kindred and go to the land I will show you.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 12:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 12:1"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 7:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Abraham"
          ]
        },
        " left ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " land of the Chaldeans ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " settled in Haran. After his father died, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " brought him out of that place ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " into this land where you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " now living."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 7:5"
        },
        "He gave him no inheritance ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "here"
          ]
        },
        ", not even a foot of ground. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " promised to give possession of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the land"
          ]
        },
        " to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Abraham"
          ]
        },
        " and his descendants, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "even though"
          ]
        },
        " he did not yet have a child. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 7:6"
        },
        "God told ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " that his descendants would be foreigners in a strange land, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " they would be enslaved and mistreated four hundred years. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 7:7"
        },
        "‘",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " I will punish the nation ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " enslaves them,’ God said, ‘and afterward they will come forth and worship Me in this place.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 15:13-14",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 15:13–14"
                  ]
                },
                "; Exodus 3:12"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 7:8"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " gave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Abraham"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " covenant of circumcision, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Abraham"
          ]
        },
        " became the father of Isaac and circumcised him on the eighth day. And Isaac ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "became the father of"
          ]
        },
        " Jacob, and Jacob of the twelve patriarchs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Joseph Sold into Egypt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GEN 37:12-30",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 37:12–30"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 7:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Because"
          ]
        },
        " the patriarchs were jealous of Joseph, they sold him as a slave into Egypt. But God was with him ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 7:10"
        },
        "and rescued him from all his troubles. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " granted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Joseph"
          ]
        },
        " favor and wisdom in the sight of Pharaoh king of Egypt, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " appointed him ruler over Egypt and all his household."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 7:11"
        },
        "Then famine and great suffering swept across Egypt and Canaan, and our fathers could not find food. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 7:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " Jacob heard that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " was grain in Egypt, he sent our fathers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "on their"
          ]
        },
        " first ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "visit"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 7:13"
        },
        "On ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " second ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "visit"
          ]
        },
        ", Joseph revealed his identity to",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Joseph was made known to "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Joseph was recognized by"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " his brothers, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " family became known to Pharaoh. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 7:14"
        },
        "Then Joseph sent for his father Jacob and all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " relatives, seventy-five in all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Israel Oppressed in Egypt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 1:8-22",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 1:8–22"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 7:15"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " Jacob went down to Egypt, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " he and our fathers died. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 7:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Their bones"
          ]
        },
        " were carried back",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "And they were carried back"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to Shechem and placed in the tomb that Abraham had bought from the sons of Hamor at Shechem for a price he paid in silver."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 7:17"
        },
        "As the time drew near for God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to fulfill"
          ]
        },
        " His promise to Abraham, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " people in Egypt increased greatly in number. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 7:18"
        },
        "Then another king, who knew nothing of Joseph, arose over Egypt. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 7:19"
        },
        "He exploited our people ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " oppressed our fathers, forcing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " to abandon their infants so they would die."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Birth and Adoption of Moses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 2:1-10",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 2:1–10"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "HEB 11:23-29",
          "content": [
            "Hebrews 11:23–29"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 7:20"
        },
        "At that time Moses was born, and he was beautiful in the sight of God.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "he was of great status in God’s eyes "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "he was no ordinary child"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "For"
          ]
        },
        " three months ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " was nurtured in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " father’s house. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 7:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " he was set outside, Pharaoh’s daughter took him and brought him up as her own son. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 7:22"
        },
        "So Moses was educated in all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " wisdom of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Egyptians and was powerful in speech and action."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Rejection and Flight of Moses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 2:11-22",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 2:11–22"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 7:23"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Moses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " forty years ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "old"
          ]
        },
        ", he decided to visit his brothers, the children of Israel. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 7:24"
        },
        "And when he saw one ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of them"
          ]
        },
        " being mistreated, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Moses"
          ]
        },
        " went to his defense and avenged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " by striking down the Egyptian who was oppressing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 7:25"
        },
        "He assumed his brothers would understand that God was using him to deliver them, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they did not"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 7:26"
        },
        "The next day he came upon ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "two Israelites who"
          ]
        },
        " were fighting, and he tried to reconcile them, saying, ‘Men, you are brothers. Why are you mistreating each other?’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 7:27"
        },
        "But the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man who"
          ]
        },
        " was abusing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " neighbor pushed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Moses"
          ]
        },
        " aside ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ‘Who made you ruler and judge over us? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 7:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " you want to kill me as you killed the Egyptian yesterday?’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 2:13-14",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 2:13–14"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 7:29"
        },
        "At this remark, Moses fled to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " land of Midian, where he lived as a foreigner ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " had two sons."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Call of Moses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 3:1-22",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 3:1–22"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 7:30"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " forty years had passed, an angel appeared to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Moses"
          ]
        },
        " in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " flames of a burning bush in the desert near Mount Sinai. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 7:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " Moses saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", he marveled at the sight. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        " he approached to look ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "more closely"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " voice of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord came ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to him"
          ]
        },
        ": ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 7:32"
        },
        "‘I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "am"
          ]
        },
        " the God of your fathers, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:32 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 3:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 3:6"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Moses trembled with fear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " did not dare to look."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 7:33"
        },
        "Then the Lord said to him, ‘Take off ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " sandals, for the place where you are standing is holy ground. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 7:34"
        },
        "I have indeed seen the oppression of My people in Egypt. I have heard their groaning and have come down to deliver them. Now come, I will send you back to Egypt.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:34 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 3:5-10",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 3:5–10"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 7:35"
        },
        "This Moses, whom they had rejected with the words, ‘Who made you ruler and judge?’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:35 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 2:14",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 2:14"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the one whom God sent to be ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " ruler and redeemer through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " angel",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:35 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Angel"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 38"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " who appeared to him in the bush. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 7:36"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " led them out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " performed wonders and signs in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " land of Egypt, at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Red Sea, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " forty years in the wilderness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 7:37"
        },
        "This is the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "same"
          ]
        },
        " Moses who told the Israelites, ‘God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:37 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 18:15",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 18:15"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 7:38"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " was in the assembly in the wilderness with the angel who spoke to him on Mount Sinai, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        " our fathers. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And"
          ]
        },
        " he received living words to pass on to us.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:38 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "NE and WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to you"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Rebellion of Israel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 32:1-35",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 32:1–35"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 9:7-29",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 9:7–29"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "AMO 5:16-27",
          "content": [
            "Amos 5:16–27"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 7:39"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " our fathers refused to obey ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". Instead, they rejected ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " and in their hearts turned back to Egypt. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 7:40"
        },
        "They said to Aaron, ‘Make us gods who will go before us! As for this Moses who led us out of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " land of Egypt, we do not know what has happened to him.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:40 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 32:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 32:1"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 7:41"
        },
        "At that time they made a calf and offered a sacrifice to the idol, rejoicing in the works of their hands. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "ACT 7:42"
        },
        "But God turned away ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from them"
          ]
        },
        " and gave them over to the worship of the host of heaven, as it is written in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " book of the prophets:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘Did you bring Me sacrifices and offerings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "ACT 7:43"
        },
        "You have taken along the tabernacle of Molech"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the star of your god Rephan,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the idols you made to worship."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Therefore"
          ]
        },
        " I will send you into exile"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "beyond Babylon.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:43 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "AMO 5:25-27",
                  "content": [
                    "Amos 5:25–27"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Tabernacle of the Testimony"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 40:1-33",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 40:1–33"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "HEB 9:1-10",
          "content": [
            "Hebrews 9:1–10"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "ACT 7:44"
        },
        "Our fathers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "had"
          ]
        },
        " the tabernacle of the Testimony with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in the wilderness. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It was"
          ]
        },
        " constructed exactly as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " had directed Moses, according to the pattern he had seen. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "ACT 7:45"
        },
        "And our fathers who received it brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it in"
          ]
        },
        " with Joshua ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they dispossessed the nations God drove out before ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It remained"
          ]
        },
        " until the time of David, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "ACT 7:46"
        },
        "who found favor in the sight of God and asked to provide a dwelling place for the God of Jacob.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:46 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "SBL, WH, BYZ, and TR; see also LXX for ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 132:5",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 132:5"
                  ]
                },
                "; ECM and NE "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "a dwelling place for the house of Jacob."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "ACT 7:47"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it was"
          ]
        },
        " Solomon ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " built ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " house for Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "ACT 7:48"
        },
        "However, the Most High ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "does"
          ]
        },
        " not dwell in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "houses"
          ]
        },
        " made by human hands. As the prophet says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "ACT 7:49"
        },
        "‘Heaven ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " My throne"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the earth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " My footstool."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "What kind of house will you build for Me, says ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "or where ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will"
          ]
        },
        " My place of repose ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "be"
          ]
        },
        "?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "ACT 7:50"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Has"
          ]
        },
        " not My hand made all these things?’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:50 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 66:1-2",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 66:1–2"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "ACT 7:51"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You"
          ]
        },
        " stiff-necked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        " uncircumcised hearts and ears! You always resist the Holy Spirit, just as your fathers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "ACT 7:52"
        },
        "Which of the prophets ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " your fathers fail to persecute? They even killed those who foretold the coming of the Righteous One. And now you are ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " betrayers and murderers — ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "53",
          "sid": "ACT 7:53"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        " who received the law ordained by angels, yet have not kept ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Stoning of Stephen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "54",
          "sid": "ACT 7:54"
        },
        "On hearing this, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the members of the Sanhedrin"
          ]
        },
        " were enraged,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:54 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "On hearing these things, they were cut in their hearts,"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and they gnashed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " teeth at him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "55",
          "sid": "ACT 7:55"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Stephen"
          ]
        },
        ", full of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit, looked intently into heaven ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " glory of God and Jesus standing at the right hand of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "56",
          "sid": "ACT 7:56"
        },
        "“Look,” he said, “I see heaven open and the Son of Man standing at the right ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "hand"
          ]
        },
        " of God.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "57",
          "sid": "ACT 7:57"
        },
        "At this they covered their ears, cried out in a loud voice, and rushed together at him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "58",
          "sid": "ACT 7:58"
        },
        "They dragged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " out of the city ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began to stone ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". Meanwhile the witnesses laid their garments at the feet of a young man named Saul."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "59",
          "sid": "ACT 7:59"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        " they were stoning ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", Stephen appealed, “Lord Jesus, receive my spirit.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "60",
          "sid": "ACT 7:60"
        },
        "Falling on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " knees, he cried out in a loud voice, “Lord, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not hold this sin against them.” And when he had said this, he fell asleep."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "8",
      "sid": "ACT 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Saul Persecutes the Church"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 8:1"
        },
        "And Saul was there, giving approval to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Stephen’s"
          ]
        },
        " death."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "On that day a great persecution broke out against the church in Jerusalem, and all except the apostles were scattered throughout Judea and Samaria. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 8:2"
        },
        "God-fearing men buried Stephen and mourned deeply over him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 8:3"
        },
        "But Saul began to destroy the church. Going from house to house, he dragged off men and women ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in prison."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Philip in Samaria"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 8:4"
        },
        "Those who had been scattered preached the word wherever they went. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 8:5"
        },
        "Philip went down to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " city ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in"
          ]
        },
        " Samaria ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " proclaimed the Christ to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 8:6"
        },
        "The crowds all paid close attention to Philip’s message and to the signs they saw him perform. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 8:7"
        },
        "With loud shrieks, unclean spirits came out of many who were possessed, and many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the"
          ]
        },
        " paralyzed and lame were healed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 8:8"
        },
        "So there was great joy in that city."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Simon the Sorcerer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 18:9-14",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 18:9–14"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 8:9"
        },
        "Prior to that time, a man named Simon had practiced sorcery in the city and astounded the people of Samaria. He claimed to be someone great, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 8:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        ", from the least to the greatest, heeded ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his words "
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " is the divine power called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Great ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Power"
          ]
        },
        ".” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 8:11"
        },
        "They paid close attention to him because he had astounded them for a long time with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " sorcery."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 8:12"
        },
        "But when they believed Philip as he preached the gospel of the kingdom of God and the name of Jesus Christ, they were baptized, both men and women. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 8:13"
        },
        "Even Simon himself believed and was baptized. He followed Philip ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "closely"
          ]
        },
        " and was astounded ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "by the"
          ]
        },
        " great signs and miracles he observed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 8:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the apostles in Jerusalem heard that Samaria had received the word of God, they sent Peter and John to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 8:15"
        },
        "On their arrival, they prayed for them to receive ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 8:16"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Holy Spirit"
          ]
        },
        " had not yet fallen upon any of them; they had simply been baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 8:17"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter and John"
          ]
        },
        " laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " hands on them, and they received ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 8:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " Simon saw that the Spirit was given through the laying on of the apostles’ hands, he offered them money. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 8:19"
        },
        "“Give ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "me"
          ]
        },
        " this power as well,” he said, “so that everyone on whom I lay ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my"
          ]
        },
        " hands may receive ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 8:20"
        },
        "But Peter replied, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "May"
          ]
        },
        " your silver perish with you, because you thought you could buy the gift of God with money! ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 8:21"
        },
        "You have no part ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " share in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " ministry, because your heart is not right before God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 8:22"
        },
        "Repent, therefore, of your wickedness, and pray to the Lord. Perhaps He will forgive you for the intent of your heart. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 8:23"
        },
        "For I see that you are poisoned by bitterness and captive to iniquity.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 8:24"
        },
        "Then Simon answered, “Pray to the Lord for me, so that nothing you have said may happen to me.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 8:25"
        },
        "And after ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter and John"
          ]
        },
        " had testified and spoken the word of the Lord, they returned to Jerusalem, preaching the gospel in many of the Samaritan villages."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Philip and the Ethiopian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 53:1-8",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 53:1–8"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 8:26"
        },
        "Now an angel of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord said to Philip, “Get up and go south to the desert road that goes down from Jerusalem to Gaza.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 8:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " he started out, and on his way ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he met"
          ]
        },
        " an Ethiopian eunuch, a court official in charge of the entire treasury of Candace,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:27 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Kandakē"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " queen of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Ethiopians. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " had gone to Jerusalem to worship, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 8:28"
        },
        "and on his return was sitting in his chariot reading Isaiah the prophet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 8:29"
        },
        "The Spirit said to Philip, “Go over to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " chariot and stay by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 8:30"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " Philip ran up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " reading Isaiah the prophet. “Do you understand what you are reading?” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Philip"
          ]
        },
        " asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 8:31"
        },
        "“How can I,” he said, “unless someone guides me?” And he invited Philip to come up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sit with him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 8:32"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The eunuch"
          ]
        },
        " was reading this passage of Scripture:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“He was led like a sheep to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " slaughter,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and as a lamb before the shearer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " silent,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "so He did not open His mouth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 8:33"
        },
        "In His humiliation He was deprived of justice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "Who can recount His descendants?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "For His life was removed from the earth.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:33 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 53:7-8",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 53:7–8"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 8:34"
        },
        "“Tell me,” said the eunuch, “who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the prophet talking about, himself or someone else?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 8:35"
        },
        "Then Philip began with this very Scripture and told him the good news about Jesus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 8:36"
        },
        "As they traveled along the road ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " came to some water, the eunuch said, “Look, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "here is"
          ]
        },
        " water! What is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " to prevent me ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " being baptized?”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:36 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR includes "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fv",
                  "content": [
                    "37"
                  ]
                },
                "And Philip said, “If you believe with all your heart, you may be baptized.” The eunuch replied, “I believe that Jesus Christ is the Son of God.”"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 8:38"
        },
        "And he gave orders to stop the chariot. Then both Philip and the eunuch went down into the water, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Philip"
          ]
        },
        " baptized him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 8:39"
        },
        "When they came up out of the water, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Spirit of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord carried Philip ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "away"
          ]
        },
        ", and the eunuch saw him no more, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " went on his way rejoicing. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 8:40"
        },
        "But Philip appeared at Azotus and traveled through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that region"
          ]
        },
        ", preaching the gospel in all the towns until he came to Caesarea."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "9",
      "sid": "ACT 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Road to Damascus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 22:1-21",
          "content": [
            "Acts 22:1–21"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 26:1-23",
          "content": [
            "Acts 26:1–23"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 9:1"
        },
        "Meanwhile, Saul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " still breathing out murderous threats against the disciples of the Lord. He approached the high priest ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 9:2"
        },
        "and requested letters to the synagogues in Damascus, so that if he found any men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " women belonging to the Way, he could bring them as prisoners to Jerusalem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 9:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        " drew near to Damascus on his journey, suddenly a light from heaven flashed around him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 9:4"
        },
        "He fell to the ground ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " heard a voice say to him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 9:5"
        },
        "“Who are You, Lord?” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        " asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting,”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He replied"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR includes "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "“It is hard for you to kick against the goads.” "
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "6",
              "sid": "ACT 9:6"
            },
            "“Now get up and go into the city, and you will be told what you must do.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 9:7"
        },
        "The men traveling with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        " stood ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " speechless. They heard the voice but did not see ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anyone"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 9:8"
        },
        "Saul got up from the ground, but when he opened his eyes he could not see ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a thing"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "he could see nothing "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "he could see no one"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they led him by the hand into Damascus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 9:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "For"
          ]
        },
        " three days he was without sight, and he did not eat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " drink ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anything"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Ananias Baptizes Saul"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 9:10"
        },
        "In Damascus there was a disciple named Ananias. The Lord spoke to him in a vision, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Ananias!”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Here I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "am"
          ]
        },
        ", Lord,” he answered."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "11",
              "sid": "ACT 9:11"
            },
            "“Get up!”"
          ]
        },
        " the Lord ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "told"
          ]
        },
        " him. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Go to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " house of Judas on Straight Street and ask for ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "a man from"
              ]
            },
            " Tarsus named Saul, for he is praying. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "12",
              "sid": "ACT 9:12"
            },
            "In a vision he has seen a man named Ananias come and place ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "his"
              ]
            },
            " hands on him to restore his sight.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 9:13"
        },
        "But Ananias answered, “Lord, many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " have told me about this man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " harm he has done to Your saints in Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 9:14"
        },
        "And now ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he is"
          ]
        },
        " here with authority from the chief priests to arrest all who call on Your name.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "15",
              "sid": "ACT 9:15"
            },
            "“Go!”"
          ]
        },
        " said the Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“This ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "man"
              ]
            },
            " is My chosen instrument to carry My name before the Gentiles and their kings, and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "before the"
              ]
            },
            " people of Israel. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "16",
              "sid": "ACT 9:16"
            },
            "I will show him how much he must suffer for My name.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 9:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " Ananias went to the house, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " he arrived, he placed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " hands on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        ". “Brother Saul,” he said, “the Lord Jesus, who appeared to you on the road ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " you were coming ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "here"
          ]
        },
        ", has sent me so that you may see again and be filled ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 9:18"
        },
        "At that instant, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "something"
          ]
        },
        " like scales fell from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul’s"
          ]
        },
        " eyes, and his sight was restored. He got up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was baptized, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 9:19"
        },
        "and after taking ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " food, he regained his strength. And he spent several days with the disciples in Damascus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Saul Preaches at Damascus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 9:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        " promptly began to proclaim Jesus in the synagogues, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "declaring "
          ]
        },
        ", “He is the Son of God.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 9:21"
        },
        "All who heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " were astounded and asked, “Isn’t this the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man who"
          ]
        },
        " wreaked havoc in Jerusalem on those ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " call on this name? And hasn’t he come here to take them as prisoners to the chief priests?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 9:22"
        },
        "But Saul was empowered all the more, and he confounded the Jews living in Damascus by proving that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " is the Christ."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Escape from Damascus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 9:23"
        },
        "After many days had passed, the Jews conspired to kill him, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 9:24"
        },
        "but Saul learned of their plot. Day and night they watched the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "city"
          ]
        },
        " gates in order to kill him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 9:25"
        },
        "One night, however, his disciples took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " lowered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " in a basket through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a window "
          ]
        },
        " in the wall.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "through the wall"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "2CO 11:33",
                  "content": [
                    "2 Corinthians 11:33"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Saul in Jerusalem"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 9:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        " arrived in Jerusalem, he tried to join the disciples, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " they were all afraid of him, not believing that he was a disciple. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 9:27"
        },
        "Then Barnabas brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to the apostles and described how ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        " had seen the Lord, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " had spoken to him on the road ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to Damascus"
          ]
        },
        ", and how ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        " had spoken boldly in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that city"
          ]
        },
        " in the name of Jesus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 9:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        " stayed with them, moving about freely in Jerusalem ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " speaking boldly in the name of the Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 9:29"
        },
        "He talked and debated with the Grecian Jews,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:29 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Hellenists"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " but they tried to kill him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 9:30"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the brothers learned of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they took him down to Caesarea and sent him off to Tarsus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Healing of Aeneas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 9:31"
        },
        "Then the church throughout Judea, Galilee, and Samaria experienced ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a time of"
          ]
        },
        " peace. It grew in strength and numbers, living in the fear of the Lord and the encouragement of the Holy Spirit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 9:32"
        },
        "As Peter traveled throughout ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the area"
          ]
        },
        ", he went to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "visit"
          ]
        },
        " the saints ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in"
          ]
        },
        " Lydda. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 9:33"
        },
        "There he found a man named Aeneas who had been paralyzed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " bedridden for eight years. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 9:34"
        },
        "“Aeneas,” Peter said to him, “Jesus Christ heals you! Get up and put away your mat.” Immediately ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Aeneas"
          ]
        },
        " got up, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 9:35"
        },
        "and all who lived in Lydda and Sharon saw him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " turned to the Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Raising of Tabitha"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 11:38-44",
          "content": [
            "John 11:38–44"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 9:36"
        },
        "In Joppa there was a disciple named Tabitha (which is translated as Dorcas),",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:36 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Tabitha "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "in Aramaic and "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Dorcas "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "in Greek both mean "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "gazelle"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " who was always occupied with works of kindness and charity. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 9:37"
        },
        "At that time, however, she became sick ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " died, and her body was washed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " placed in an upper room. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 9:38"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Since"
          ]
        },
        " Lydda was near Joppa, the disciples, hearing that Peter was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ", sent two men to urge him, “Come to us without delay.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 9:39"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " Peter got up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went with them. On his arrival, they took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to the upper room. All the widows stood around him, weeping and showing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " tunics and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "other"
          ]
        },
        " clothing that Dorcas had made while she was still with them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 9:40"
        },
        "Then Peter sent them all out of the room. He knelt down ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " prayed, and turning toward ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her"
          ]
        },
        " body, he said, “Tabitha, get up!” She opened her eyes, and seeing Peter, she sat up. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 9:41"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " took her by the hand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " helped her up. Then he called the saints and widows ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " presented her ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to them"
          ]
        },
        " alive."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "ACT 9:42"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This"
          ]
        },
        " became known all over Joppa, and many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " believed in the Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "ACT 9:43"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " stayed for several days in Joppa with a tanner ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "named"
          ]
        },
        " Simon."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "10",
      "sid": "ACT 10"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Cornelius Sends for Peter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 10:1"
        },
        "At Caesarea ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there was"
          ]
        },
        " a man named Cornelius, a centurion in what was called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Italian Regiment. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 10:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He and"
          ]
        },
        " all his household ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " devout and God-fearing. He gave generously to the people and prayed to God regularly. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 10:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " day at about the ninth hour,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, about three in the afternoon; also in verse 30"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " he had a clear vision of an angel of God who came to him and said, “Cornelius!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 10:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Cornelius"
          ]
        },
        " stared at him in fear and asked, “What is it, Lord?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The angel"
          ]
        },
        " answered, “Your prayers and gifts to the poor have ascended as a memorial ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "offering "
          ]
        },
        " before God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 10:5"
        },
        "Now send men to Joppa to call for a man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "named"
          ]
        },
        " Simon who is called Peter. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 10:6"
        },
        "He is staying with Simon ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " tanner, whose house is by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sea.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR includes "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "He will tell you what you need to do."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 10:7"
        },
        "When the angel who spoke to him had gone, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Cornelius"
          ]
        },
        " called two of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " servants and a devout soldier from among his attendants. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 10:8"
        },
        "He explained what had happened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sent them to Joppa."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter’s Vision"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "LEV 11:1-47",
          "content": [
            "Leviticus 11:1–47"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 14:1-21",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 14:1–21"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 10:9"
        },
        "The next day at about the sixth hour,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:9 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, about noon"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the men"
          ]
        },
        " were approaching the city on their journey, Peter went up on the roof to pray. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 10:10"
        },
        "He became hungry and wanted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "something"
          ]
        },
        " to eat, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "while"
          ]
        },
        " the meal was being prepared, he fell into a trance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 10:11"
        },
        "He saw heaven open and something like a large sheet being let down to earth by its four corners. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 10:12"
        },
        "It contained all kinds of four-footed animals and reptiles of the earth, as well as birds of the air. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 10:13"
        },
        "Then a voice said to him: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Get up, Peter, kill and eat!”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 10:14"
        },
        "“No, Lord!” Peter answered. “I have never eaten anything impure",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "common"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; similarly in verses 15 and 28"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " or unclean.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 10:15"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " voice ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "spoke"
          ]
        },
        " to him a second time: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 10:16"
        },
        "This happened three times, and all at once the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "sheet"
          ]
        },
        " was taken back up into heaven."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter Called to Caesarea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 10:17"
        },
        "While Peter was puzzling over the meaning of the vision, the men sent by Cornelius found Simon’s house ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " approached the gate. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 10:18"
        },
        "They called out to ask if Simon called Peter was staying ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 10:19"
        },
        "As Peter continued to reflect on the vision, the Spirit said to him, “Behold, three men are looking for you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "ECM and TR; NE and WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "two men are looking for you"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; SBL and BYZ "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "men are looking for you"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 10:20"
        },
        "So get up! Go downstairs and accompany them without hesitation, because I have sent them.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 10:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " Peter went down to the men",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the men sent to him by Cornelius"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Here am I, the one you are looking for. Why have you come?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 10:22"
        },
        "“Cornelius ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " centurion ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "has sent us "
          ]
        },
        ",” they said. “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He is"
          ]
        },
        " a righteous and God-fearing man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        " a good reputation among the whole Jewish nation. A holy angel instructed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to request your presence in his home ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so he could"
          ]
        },
        " hear a message from you.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 10:23"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " invited them in as his guests. And the next day he got ready ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went with them, accompanied by some of the brothers from Joppa."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter Visits Cornelius"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 10:24"
        },
        "The following day he arrived in Caesarea, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " Cornelius was expecting them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " had called together his relatives and close friends. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 10:25"
        },
        "As Peter was about to enter, Cornelius met him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " fell at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " feet to worship ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 10:26"
        },
        "But Peter helped him up. “Stand up,” he said, “I am only a man myself.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 10:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " talked with him, he went inside and found many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " gathered together. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 10:28"
        },
        "He said to them, “You know how unlawful it is for a Jew to associate with a foreigner or visit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". But God has shown me ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " I should not call ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "any"
          ]
        },
        " man impure or unclean. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 10:29"
        },
        "So when I was invited, I came without objection. I ask, then, why have you sent for me?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 10:30"
        },
        "Cornelius answered: “Four days ago I was in my house praying at this, the ninth hour.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:30 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Four days ago I was fasting until this hour, and at the ninth hour I was praying in my house."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Suddenly a man in radiant clothing stood before me ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 10:31"
        },
        "and said, ‘Cornelius, your prayer has been heard, and your gifts to the poor have been remembered before God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 10:32"
        },
        "Therefore send to Joppa for Simon, who is called Peter. He is a guest in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " home of Simon ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " tanner, by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sea.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 10:33"
        },
        "So I sent for you immediately, and you were kind enough to come. Now then, we ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " all here in the presence of God to listen to everything the Lord has instructed you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to tell us"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Good News for the Gentiles"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 10:34"
        },
        "Then Peter began to speak: “I now truly understand that God does not show favoritism, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 10:35"
        },
        "but welcomes those from every nation who fear Him and do what is right. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 10:36"
        },
        "He has sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " message to the people of Israel, proclaiming the gospel of peace through Jesus Christ, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " is Lord of all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 10:37"
        },
        "You yourselves know what has happened throughout Judea, beginning in Galilee with the baptism that John proclaimed: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 10:38"
        },
        "how God anointed Jesus of Nazareth with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit and with power, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " how ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " went around doing good and healing all who were oppressed by the devil, because God was with Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 10:39"
        },
        "We ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " witnesses of all that He did, both in the land of the Jews and in Jerusalem. And although they put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " to death by hanging ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " on a tree, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 10:40"
        },
        "God raised ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " up on the third day and caused Him to be seen — ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 10:41"
        },
        "not by all the people, but by the witnesses God had chosen beforehand, by us who ate and drank with Him after He rose from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "ACT 10:42"
        },
        "And He commanded us to preach to the people and to testify that He is the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " appointed by God to judge ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " living and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "ACT 10:43"
        },
        "All the prophets testify about Him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " everyone who believes in Him receives forgiveness of sins through His name.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Gentiles Receive the Holy Spirit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 19:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Acts 19:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "ACT 10:44"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        " Peter was still speaking these words, the Holy Spirit fell upon all who heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " message. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "ACT 10:45"
        },
        "All the circumcised believers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " had accompanied Peter were astounded that the gift of the Holy Spirit had been poured out even on the Gentiles. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "ACT 10:46"
        },
        "For they heard them speaking in tongues and exalting God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Then Peter said, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "ACT 10:47"
        },
        "“Can anyone withhold the water to baptize these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        "? ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They"
          ]
        },
        " have received the Holy Spirit just as we ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "have"
          ]
        },
        "!” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "ACT 10:48"
        },
        "So he ordered that they be baptized in the name of Jesus Christ. Then they asked him to stay ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for a few"
          ]
        },
        " days."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "11",
      "sid": "ACT 11"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Peter’s Report at Jerusalem"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 11:1"
        },
        "The apostles and brothers throughout Judea soon heard that the Gentiles also had received the word of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 11:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " when Peter went up to Jerusalem, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " circumcised ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "believers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "those of the circumcision"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " took issue with him ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 11:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “You visited uncircumcised men and ate with them.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 11:4"
        },
        "But Peter began ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " explained to them the whole sequence of events: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 11:5"
        },
        "“I was in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " city of Joppa praying, and in a trance I saw a vision ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " something like a large sheet being let down from heaven by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " four corners, and it came right down to me. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 11:6"
        },
        "I looked at it ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "closely"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " saw four-footed animals of the earth, wild beasts, reptiles, and birds of the air. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 11:7"
        },
        "Then I heard a voice saying to me, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Get up, Peter, kill and eat.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 11:8"
        },
        "‘No, Lord,’ I said, ‘for nothing impure",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "common"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; similarly in verse 9"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " or unclean has ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "ever"
          ]
        },
        " entered my mouth.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 11:9"
        },
        "But the voice spoke from heaven a second ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "time"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 11:10"
        },
        "This happened three times, and everything was drawn back up into heaven."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 11:11"
        },
        "Just then three men sent to me from Caesarea stopped at the house ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " I was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "staying"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 11:12"
        },
        "The Spirit told me to accompany them without hesitation. These six brothers also went with me, and we entered the man’s home. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 11:13"
        },
        "He told us how he had seen an angel standing in his house and saying, ‘Send to Joppa ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " Simon who is called Peter. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 11:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " will convey to you a message by which you and all your household will be saved.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 11:15"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        " I began to speak, the Holy Spirit fell upon them, just as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He had fallen"
          ]
        },
        " upon us at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " beginning. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 11:16"
        },
        "Then I remembered the word of the Lord, how He said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘John baptized with water, but you will be baptized with ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Holy Spirit.’",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "11:16 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    "Or "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fqa",
                  "content": [
                    "‘John baptized in water, but in a few days you will be baptized in the Holy Spirit.’"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "ACT 1:5",
                      "content": [
                        "Acts 1:5"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 11:17"
        },
        "So if God gave them the same gift ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He gave"
          ]
        },
        " us who believed in the Lord Jesus Christ, who was I to hinder ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the work of"
          ]
        },
        " God?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 11:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they had no further ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "objections"
          ]
        },
        ", and they glorified God, saying, “So then, God has granted even the Gentiles repentance unto life.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Church at Antioch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 11:19"
        },
        "Meanwhile those scattered by the persecution that began with Stephen traveled as far as Phoenicia, Cyprus, and Antioch, speaking the message only to Jews. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 11:20"
        },
        "But some of them, men from Cyprus and Cyrene, went to Antioch and began speaking to the Greeks",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Hellenists"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " as well, proclaiming the good news about the Lord Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 11:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " hand of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord was with them, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " great number ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of people"
          ]
        },
        " believed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " turned to the Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 11:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " news of this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "reached"
          ]
        },
        " the ears of the church in Jerusalem, they sent Barnabas to Antioch. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 11:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " he arrived and saw the grace of God, he rejoiced and encouraged them all to abide in the Lord with all their hearts. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 11:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Barnabas"
          ]
        },
        " was a good man, full of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit and faith, and a great ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "number of people"
          ]
        },
        " were brought to the Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 11:25"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Barnabas"
          ]
        },
        " went to Tarsus to look for Saul, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 11:26"
        },
        "and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " he found ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", he brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " back to Antioch. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " a full year they met together with the church and taught large ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "numbers of people"
          ]
        },
        ". The disciples were first called Christians at Antioch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 11:27"
        },
        "In those days ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " prophets came down from Jerusalem to Antioch. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 11:28"
        },
        "One of them named Agabus stood up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " predicted through the Spirit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " a great famine would sweep across the whole world.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the entire Roman world"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " (",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This"
          ]
        },
        " happened under Claudius.) ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 11:29"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " the disciples, each according to his ability, decided to send relief to the brothers living in Judea. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 11:30"
        },
        "This they did, sending ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their gifts"
          ]
        },
        " to the elders with Barnabas and Saul."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "12",
      "sid": "ACT 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "James Killed, Peter Imprisoned"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 12:1"
        },
        "About that time, King Herod",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, King Herod Agrippa"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " reached out to harm",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "put forth the hands to mistreat"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " some who belonged to the church. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 12:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He had"
          ]
        },
        " James, the brother of John, put to death with the sword."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 12:3"
        },
        "And seeing that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " pleased the Jews, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Herod"
          ]
        },
        " proceeded to seize Peter during the Feast of Unleavened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Bread"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "seize Peter—now these were the days of the Unleavened"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 12:14-20",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 12:14–20"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 12:4"
        },
        "He arrested ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " and put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " in prison, handing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " over to be guarded by four squads of four soldiers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "each"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Herod"
          ]
        },
        " intended to bring him out to the people after the Passover."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Rescue of Peter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 12:5"
        },
        "So Peter was kept in prison, but the church was fervently praying to God for him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 12:6"
        },
        "On ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " night ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "before"
          ]
        },
        " Herod was to bring him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to trial"
          ]
        },
        ", Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, bound with two chains, with sentries standing guard at the entrance to the prison. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 12:7"
        },
        "Suddenly an angel of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord appeared and a light shone in the cell. He tapped Peter on the side ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " woke him up, saying, “Get up quickly.” And the chains fell off ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " wrists. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 12:8"
        },
        "“Get dressed and put on your sandals,” said the angel. Peter did so, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the angel"
          ]
        },
        " told him, “Wrap your cloak ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "around you"
          ]
        },
        " and follow me.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 12:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " followed him out, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " he was unaware that what the angel was doing was real. He thought he was only seeing a vision. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 12:10"
        },
        "They passed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " first and second guards ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " came to the iron gate leading to the city, which opened for them by itself. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they had gone outside ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " walked the length of one block, the angel suddenly left him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 12:11"
        },
        "Then Peter came to himself ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Now I know for sure that the Lord has sent His angel and rescued me from Herod’s grasp and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " everything the Jewish people were anticipating.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 12:12"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " he had realized ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", he went to the house of Mary the mother of John, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "also"
          ]
        },
        " called Mark, where many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " had gathered together and were praying. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 12:13"
        },
        "He knocked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "at"
          ]
        },
        " the outer gate, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " a servant girl named Rhoda came to answer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 12:14"
        },
        "When she recognized Peter’s voice, she was so overjoyed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " she forgot to open the gate, but ran inside ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " announced, “Peter is standing at the gate!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 12:15"
        },
        "“You are out of your mind,” they told her. But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " she kept insisting ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " was so, they said, “It must be his angel.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 12:16"
        },
        "But Peter kept on knocking, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they opened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the door"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " saw him, they were astounded. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 12:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Peter"
          ]
        },
        " motioned with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " hand for silence, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " he described how the Lord had brought him out of the prison. “Send word to James and to the brothers,” he said, and he left for another place."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 12:18"
        },
        "At daybreak there was no small commotion among the soldiers as to what had become ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " Peter. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 12:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " Herod had searched for him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "unsuccessfully"
          ]
        },
        ", he examined the guards ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ordered that they be executed. Then he went down from Judea to Caesarea ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " spent some time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Death of Herod"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 12:20"
        },
        "Now ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Herod"
          ]
        },
        " was in a furious dispute",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "had become furious "
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with the"
          ]
        },
        " people of Tyre and Sidon, and they convened before him. Having secured the support of Blastus, the king’s chamberlain, they asked for peace, because their region depended on the king’s ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "country"
          ]
        },
        " for food. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 12:21"
        },
        "On the appointed day, Herod donned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " royal ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "robes"
          ]
        },
        ", sat on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " throne, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " addressed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 12:22"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they"
          ]
        },
        " began to shout, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This is the"
          ]
        },
        " voice of a god, not a man!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 12:23"
        },
        "Immediately, because ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Herod"
          ]
        },
        " did not give glory to God, an angel of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord struck him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "down"
          ]
        },
        ", and he was eaten by worms ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " died."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 12:24"
        },
        "But the word of God continued to spread and multiply."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 12:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " Barnabas and Saul had fulfilled ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " mission to Jerusalem, they returned,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "had fulfilled their mission, they returned to Jerusalem"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; NE and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "had fulfilled their mission, they returned from Jerusalem"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " bringing with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " John, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "also"
          ]
        },
        " called Mark."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "13",
      "sid": "ACT 13"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s First Missionary Journey Begins"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 15:36-41",
          "content": [
            "Acts 15:36–41"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 18:23-28",
          "content": [
            "Acts 18:23–28"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 13:1"
        },
        "Now in the church at Antioch there were prophets and teachers: Barnabas, Simeon called Niger, Lucius of Cyrene, Manaen (who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch), and Saul. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 13:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        " they were worshiping the Lord and fasting, the Holy Spirit said, “Set apart for Me Barnabas and Saul for the work to which I have called them.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 13:3"
        },
        "And after they had fasted and prayed, they laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " hands on them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " off."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "On Cyprus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 13:4"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Barnabas and Saul"
          ]
        },
        ", sent forth by the Holy Spirit, went down to Seleucia and sailed from there to Cyprus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 13:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they arrived at Salamis, they proclaimed the word of God in the Jewish synagogues. And John was with them as their helper."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 13:6"
        },
        "They traveled through the whole island as far as Paphos, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " they found a Jewish sorcerer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " false prophet named Bar-Jesus, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 13:7"
        },
        "an attendant of the proconsul, Sergius Paulus. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The proconsul"
          ]
        },
        ", a man of intelligence, summoned Barnabas and Saul because he wanted to hear the word of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 13:8"
        },
        "But Elymas the sorcerer (for that is what his name means) opposed them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " tried to turn the proconsul from the faith."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 13:9"
        },
        "Then Saul, who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " also ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "called"
          ]
        },
        " Paul, filled with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit, looked directly at Elymas ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 13:10"
        },
        "and said, “O child of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " devil ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " enemy of all righteousness, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you are"
          ]
        },
        " full of all kinds of deceit and trickery! Will you never stop perverting the straight ways of the Lord? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 13:11"
        },
        "Now look, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " hand of the Lord ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " against you, and for a time you will be blind ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " unable to see the light of the sun.” Immediately mist and darkness came over him, and he groped about, seeking someone to lead ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " by the hand."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 13:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the proconsul saw what had happened, he believed, for he was astonished at the teaching about the Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "In Pisidian Antioch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 13:13"
        },
        "After setting sail from Paphos, Paul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " his companions came to Perga in Pamphylia, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " John left them to return to Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 13:14"
        },
        "And from Perga, they traveled inland to Pisidian Antioch, where they entered the synagogue on the Sabbath ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sat down. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 13:15"
        },
        "After the reading from the Law and the Prophets, the synagogue leaders sent word to them: “Brothers, if you have a word of encouragement for the people, please speak.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 13:16"
        },
        "Paul stood up, motioned with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " hand, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began to speak: “Men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " Israel and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you Gentiles"
          ]
        },
        " who fear God, listen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to me"
          ]
        },
        "! ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 13:17"
        },
        "The God of the people of Israel chose our fathers. He made them into a great people during ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " stay in Egypt, and with an uplifted arm He led them out of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that land"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 13:18"
        },
        "He endured their conduct for about forty years in the wilderness. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 13:19"
        },
        "And having vanquished seven nations in Canaan, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He gave"
          ]
        },
        " their land ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to His people"
          ]
        },
        " as an inheritance. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 13:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "All this took about"
          ]
        },
        " 450 years."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "After this, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " gave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " judges until the time of Samuel the prophet. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 13:21"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " asked for a king, and God gave them Saul son of Kish, from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " tribe of Benjamin, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who ruled"
          ]
        },
        " forty years. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 13:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " removing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Saul"
          ]
        },
        ", He raised up David as their king and testified ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "about him"
          ]
        },
        ": ‘I have found David ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "son"
          ]
        },
        " of Jesse a man after My ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " heart; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " will carry out My will in its entirety.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "1SA 13:14",
                  "content": [
                    "1 Samuel 13:14"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 13:23"
        },
        "From the descendants of this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        ", God has brought to Israel ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Savior Jesus, as He promised. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 13:24"
        },
        "Before the arrival of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", John preached a baptism of repentance to all the people of Israel. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 13:25"
        },
        "As John was completing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " course, he said, ‘Who do you suppose I am? I am not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that One"
          ]
        },
        ". But there is One coming after me whose sandals I am not worthy to untie.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "LUK 3:16",
                  "content": [
                    "Luke 3:16"
                  ]
                },
                "; see also Matthew 3:11, Mark 1:7, and John 1:27."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 13:26"
        },
        "Brothers, children of Abraham, and you  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Gentiles "
          ]
        },
        " who fear God, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " to us ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " this message of salvation has been sent. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 13:27"
        },
        "The ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " of Jerusalem and their rulers did not recognize ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", yet in condemning ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " they fulfilled the words of the prophets that are read every Sabbath. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 13:28"
        },
        "And though they found no ground for a death sentence, they asked Pilate to have Him executed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 13:29"
        },
        "When they had carried out all that was written about Him, they took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " down from the tree ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " in a tomb. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 13:30"
        },
        "But God raised Him from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 13:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " for many days ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " was seen by those who had accompanied Him from Galilee to Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They"
          ]
        },
        " are now His witnesses to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 13:32"
        },
        "And now we proclaim to you the good news: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "What God"
          ]
        },
        " promised ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " fathers ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 13:33"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " has fulfilled for us, their children, by raising up Jesus. As it is written in the second Psalm:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘You are My Son;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "today I have become Your Father.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:33 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 2:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 2:7"
                  ]
                },
                "; literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "today I have begotten You"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 13:34"
        },
        "In fact, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " raised Him from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, never to see decay. As He has said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘I will give you the holy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sure ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "blessings"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "promised to"
          ]
        },
        " David.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:34 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "I will give you the holy, the trustworthy of David"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 55:3",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 55:3"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 13:35"
        },
        "So also, He says in another ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Psalm"
          ]
        },
        ":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘You will not let Your Holy One see decay.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:35 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 16:10",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 16:10"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 13:36"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " David had served God’s purpose in his own generation, he fell asleep. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His body"
          ]
        },
        " was buried with his fathers and saw decay. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 13:37"
        },
        "But the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " whom God raised from the dead did not see decay."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 13:38"
        },
        "Therefore let it be known to you, brothers, that through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " forgiveness of sins is proclaimed to you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 13:39"
        },
        "Through Him everyone who believes is justified from everything from which you could not be justified by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law of Moses. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 13:40"
        },
        "Watch out, then, that what was spoken by the prophets does not happen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to you"
          ]
        },
        ":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 13:41"
        },
        "‘Look, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        " scoffers,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "wonder and perish!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "For I am doing a work in your days"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " you would never believe,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "even if someone told you.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:41 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HAB 1:5",
                  "content": [
                    "Habakkuk 1:5"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Light for the Gentiles"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 49:1-6",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 49:1–6"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "ACT 13:42"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Barnabas"
          ]
        },
        " were leaving ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the synagogue"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " urged them to continue this message on the next Sabbath. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "ACT 13:43"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " the synagogue was dismissed, many of the Jews and devout converts to Judaism followed Paul and Barnabas, who spoke to them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " urged them to continue in the grace of God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "ACT 13:44"
        },
        "On the following Sabbath, nearly the whole city gathered to hear the word of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "45",
          "sid": "ACT 13:45"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " the Jews saw the crowds, they were filled with jealousy, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they"
          ]
        },
        " blasphemously contradicted what Paul was saying."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "46",
          "sid": "ACT 13:46"
        },
        "Then Paul and Barnabas answered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " boldly: “It was necessary to speak the word of God to you first. But since you reject it and do not consider yourselves worthy of eternal life, we now turn to the Gentiles. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "47",
          "sid": "ACT 13:47"
        },
        "For this is what the Lord has commanded us:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘I have made you a light for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Gentiles,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "to bring salvation to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " ends of the earth.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:47 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 49:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 49:6"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "48",
          "sid": "ACT 13:48"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the Gentiles heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they rejoiced and glorified the word of the Lord, and all who were appointed for eternal life believed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "49",
          "sid": "ACT 13:49"
        },
        "And the word of the Lord spread throughout ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " region."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "50",
          "sid": "ACT 13:50"
        },
        "The Jews, however, incited the religious women of prominence and the leading men of the city. They stirred up persecution against Paul and Barnabas and drove them out of their district. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "51",
          "sid": "ACT 13:51"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they shook the dust ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "off"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " feet ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in protest"
          ]
        },
        " against them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went to Iconium. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "52",
          "sid": "ACT 13:52"
        },
        "And the disciples were filled with joy and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "14",
      "sid": "ACT 14"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul and Barnabas at Iconium"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 14:1"
        },
        "At Iconium, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Barnabas"
          ]
        },
        " went as usual into the Jewish synagogue, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " they spoke so ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "well "
          ]
        },
        " that a great number of Jews and Greeks believed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 14:2"
        },
        "But the unbelieving Jews stirred up the Gentiles and poisoned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " minds against the brothers. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 14:3"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Barnabas"
          ]
        },
        " spent considerable time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ", speaking boldly for the Lord, who affirmed the message of His grace by enabling them to perform signs and wonders."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 14:4"
        },
        "The people of the city were divided. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Some"
          ]
        },
        " sided with the Jews, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "others"
          ]
        },
        " with the apostles. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 14:5"
        },
        "But when the Gentiles and Jews, together with their rulers, set out to mistreat and stone them, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 14:6"
        },
        "they found out about it and fled to the Lycaonian cities of Lystra and Derbe and to the surrounding region, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 14:7"
        },
        "where they continued to preach the gospel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Visit to Lystra and Derbe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 14:8"
        },
        "In Lystra there sat a man crippled in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " feet, who was lame from birth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "had"
          ]
        },
        " never walked. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 14:9"
        },
        "This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " was listening to the words of Paul, who looked intently at him and saw that he had faith to be healed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 14:10"
        },
        "In a loud voice ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " called out, “Stand up on your feet!” And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        " jumped up and began to walk."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 14:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the crowds saw what Paul had done, they lifted up their voices in the Lycaonian language: “The gods have come down to us in human form!” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 14:12"
        },
        "Barnabas they called Zeus, and Paul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they called"
          ]
        },
        " Hermes, because he was the chief speaker. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 14:13"
        },
        "The priest of Zeus, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "whose temple"
          ]
        },
        " was just outside the city, brought bulls and wreaths to the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "city"
          ]
        },
        " gates, hoping to offer a sacrifice along with the crowds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 14:14"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " the apostles Barnabas and Paul found out about this, they tore their clothes ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " rushed into the crowd, shouting, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 14:15"
        },
        "“Men, why are you doing this? We too are ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "only"
          ]
        },
        " men, human like you. We are bringing you good news that you should turn from these worthless things to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " living God, who made heaven and earth and sea and everything in them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 14:16"
        },
        "In past generations, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " let all nations go their ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " way. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 14:17"
        },
        "Yet He has not left Himself without testimony to His goodness: He gives you rain from heaven and fruitful seasons, filling your hearts with food and gladness.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 14:18"
        },
        "Even with these words, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Barnabas"
          ]
        },
        " could hardly stop the crowds from sacrificing to them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 14:19"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " Jews arrived from Antioch and Iconium and won over the crowds. They stoned Paul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " dragged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " outside the city, presuming he was dead. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 14:20"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "after"
          ]
        },
        " the disciples had gathered around him, he got up and went back into the city. And the next day he left with Barnabas for Derbe."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Strengthening the Disciples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 14:21"
        },
        "They preached the gospel to that city and made many disciples. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Then"
          ]
        },
        " they returned to Lystra, Iconium, and Antioch, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 14:22"
        },
        "strengthening the souls of the disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " encouraging ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " to continue in the faith. “We must endure many hardships to enter the kingdom of God,” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they said"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 14:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Barnabas"
          ]
        },
        " appointed elders for them in each church, praying ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " fasting as they entrusted them to the Lord, in whom they had believed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 14:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " passing through Pisidia, they came to Pamphylia. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 14:25"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they had spoken the word in Perga, they went down to Attalia."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 14:26"
        },
        "From ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Attalia"
          ]
        },
        " they sailed to Antioch, where they had been commended to the grace of God for the work they had just completed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 14:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they arrived, they gathered the church ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "together"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " reported all that God had done through them, and how He had opened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " door of faith to the Gentiles. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 14:28"
        },
        "And they spent a long time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " with the disciples."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "15",
      "sid": "ACT 15"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Dispute over Circumcision"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 15:1"
        },
        "Then some men came down from Judea ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " were teaching the brothers, “Unless you are circumcised according to the custom of Moses, you cannot be saved.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 15:2"
        },
        "And after engaging ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these men"
          ]
        },
        " in sharp debate, Paul and Barnabas were appointed, along with some other ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "believers "
          ]
        },
        ", to go up to Jerusalem to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "see"
          ]
        },
        " the apostles and elders about this question."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 15:3"
        },
        "Sent on their way by the church, they passed through Phoenicia and Samaria, recounting the conversion of the Gentiles and bringing great joy to all the brothers. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 15:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "On"
          ]
        },
        " their arrival in Jerusalem, they were welcomed by the church and apostles and elders, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to whom"
          ]
        },
        " they reported all that God had done through them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Council at Jerusalem"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "AMO 9:11-15",
          "content": [
            "Amos 9:11–15"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GAL 2:1-10",
          "content": [
            "Galatians 2:1–10"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 15:5"
        },
        "But some believers from the party of the Pharisees stood up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " declared, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The Gentiles"
          ]
        },
        " must be circumcised and required to obey the law of Moses.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 15:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " the apostles and elders met to look into this matter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 15:7"
        },
        "After much discussion, Peter got up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said to them, “Brothers, you know that in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " early days God made a choice among you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " the Gentiles would hear from my lips the message of the gospel and believe. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 15:8"
        },
        "And God, who knows the heart, showed His approval by giving the Holy Spirit to them, just as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He did"
          ]
        },
        " to us. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 15:9"
        },
        "He made no distinction between us and them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " He cleansed their hearts by faith."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 15:10"
        },
        "Now then, why do you test God by placing on the necks of the disciples a yoke that neither we nor our fathers have been able to bear? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 15:11"
        },
        "On the contrary, we believe ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " through the grace of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord Jesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " we are saved, just as they ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 15:12"
        },
        "The whole assembly fell silent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as they"
          ]
        },
        " listened to Barnabas and Paul describing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " signs and wonders God had done among the Gentiles through them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 15:13"
        },
        "When they had finished speaking, James declared, “Brothers, listen to me! ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 15:14"
        },
        "Simon",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "15:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Simeon"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                ", a variant of Simon"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " has told us how God first visited ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Gentiles"
          ]
        },
        " to take from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " a people ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to be"
          ]
        },
        " His ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 15:15"
        },
        "The words of the prophets agree with this, as it is written:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 15:16"
        },
        "‘After ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " I will return and rebuild"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "the fallen tent of David."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Its ruins I will rebuild,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and I will restore it,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 15:17"
        },
        "so that the remnant of men may seek the Lord,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and all the Gentiles who are called by My name,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "says ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord who does these things"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 15:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " have been known for ages.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "15:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "AMO 9:11-12",
                  "content": [
                    "Amos 9:11–12"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX); BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "says the Lord, who does all these things. ",
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fv",
                  "content": [
                    "18"
                  ]
                },
                "Known unto God are all His works from the ages."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 15:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " my judgment, therefore, that we should not cause trouble for the Gentiles ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " are turning to God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 15:20"
        },
        "Instead, we should write  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and tell"
          ]
        },
        " them to abstain from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "food "
          ]
        },
        " polluted by idols, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " sexual immorality, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " the meat of strangled animals, and from blood. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 15:21"
        },
        "For Moses has been proclaimed in every city from ancient times ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " is read in the synagogues on every Sabbath.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Letter to the Gentile Believers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 15:22"
        },
        "Then the apostles and elders, with the whole church, decided to select men from among them to send to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They chose"
          ]
        },
        " Judas called Barsabbas and Silas, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "two"
          ]
        },
        " leaders among the brothers, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 15:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and sent them with"
          ]
        },
        " this letter:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        "The apostles and the elders, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " brothers,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        "To the brothers among ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Gentiles in Antioch, Syria, and Cilicia:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        "Greetings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 15:24"
        },
        "It has come to our attention that some went out from us without our authorization ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " unsettled you, troubling your minds by what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they"
          ]
        },
        " said.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "15:24 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "by saying that you must be circumcised and keep the law."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 15:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " we all agreed to choose men to send to you along with our beloved Barnabas and Paul, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 15:26"
        },
        "men who have risked their lives for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 15:27"
        },
        "Therefore we are sending Judas and Silas to tell you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in person"
          ]
        },
        " the same things ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we are writing"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 15:28"
        },
        "It seemed good to the Holy Spirit and to us not to burden you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with anything"
          ]
        },
        " beyond these essential requirements: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 15:29"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You must"
          ]
        },
        " abstain from food sacrificed to idols, from blood, from the meat of strangled animals, and from sexual immorality. You will do well to avoid these things."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        "Farewell."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Believers at Antioch Rejoice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 15:30"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the men"
          ]
        },
        " were sent off ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went down to Antioch, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " they assembled the congregation ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " delivered the letter. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 15:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " read ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", they rejoiced at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " encouraging message."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 15:32"
        },
        "Judas and Silas, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " themselves were prophets, said much to encourage and strengthen the brothers. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 15:33"
        },
        "After spending some time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ", they were sent off by the brothers in peace to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "return to"
          ]
        },
        " those who had sent them.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "15:33 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR includes "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fv",
                  "content": [
                    "34"
                  ]
                },
                "Silas, however, decided to remain there."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 15:35"
        },
        "But Paul and Barnabas remained at Antioch, along with many others, teaching and preaching the word of the Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Second Missionary Journey Begins"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 13:1-3",
          "content": [
            "Acts 13:1–3"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 18:23-28",
          "content": [
            "Acts 18:23–28"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 15:36"
        },
        "Some time later Paul said to Barnabas, “Let us go back ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " visit the brothers in every town where we proclaimed the word of the Lord, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to see "
          ]
        },
        " how they are doing.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 15:37"
        },
        "Barnabas wanted to take John, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "also"
          ]
        },
        " called Mark. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 15:38"
        },
        "But Paul thought it best not to take him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "because"
          ]
        },
        " he had deserted them in Pamphylia and had not accompanied them in the work."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 15:39"
        },
        "Their disagreement was so sharp that they parted company. Barnabas took Mark ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sailed for Cyprus, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 15:40"
        },
        "but Paul chose Silas ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " left, commended by the brothers to the grace of the Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 15:41"
        },
        "And he traveled through Syria and Cilicia, strengthening the churches."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "16",
      "sid": "ACT 16"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Timothy Joins Paul and Silas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 16:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " came to Derbe and then to Lystra, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he found"
          ]
        },
        " a disciple named Timothy, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " son of a believing Jewish woman and a Greek father. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 16:2"
        },
        "The brothers in Lystra and Iconium spoke well of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 16:3"
        },
        "Paul wanted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Timothy"
          ]
        },
        " to accompany him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so"
          ]
        },
        " he took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " circumcised him on account of the Jews in that area, for they all knew that his father was a Greek."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 16:4"
        },
        "As they went from town to town, they delivered the decisions handed down by the apostles and elders in Jerusalem for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " to obey. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 16:5"
        },
        "So the churches were strengthened in the faith and grew daily in numbers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Vision of the Macedonian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 16:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " the Holy Spirit had prevented them from speaking the word in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in Asia"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. "
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " they traveled through the region of Phrygia and Galatia. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 16:7"
        },
        "And when they came to the border of Mysia, they tried to enter Bithynia, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " the Spirit of Jesus would not permit them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 16:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they passed by Mysia ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went down to Troas."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 16:9"
        },
        "During the night, Paul had a vision of a man of Macedonia standing and pleading with him, “Come over to Macedonia ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " help us.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 16:10"
        },
        "As soon as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " had seen the vision, we got ready to leave for Macedonia, concluding that God had called us to preach the gospel to them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Lydia’s Conversion in Philippi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "REV 2:18-29",
          "content": [
            "Revelation 2:18–29"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 16:11"
        },
        "We sailed from Troas straight to Samothrace, and the following day on to Neapolis. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 16:12"
        },
        "From there ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we went"
          ]
        },
        " to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Roman"
          ]
        },
        " colony of Philippi, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " leading city of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " district of Macedonia.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "we went to Philippi, which is a leading city of the district of Macedonia—a colony"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " And we stayed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "several"
          ]
        },
        " days."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 16:13"
        },
        "On the Sabbath we went outside the city gate along ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " river, where ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " was customary to find ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a place of"
          ]
        },
        " prayer. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " sitting down, we spoke to the women who had gathered ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 16:14"
        },
        "Among those listening ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " a woman named Lydia, a dealer in purple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "cloth"
          ]
        },
        " from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " city of Thyatira, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who was"
          ]
        },
        " a worshiper of God. The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paul’s message. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 16:15"
        },
        "And when ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "she"
          ]
        },
        " and her household had been baptized, she urged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        ", “If you consider me a believer in the Lord, come ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " stay at my house.” And she persuaded us."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul and Silas Imprisoned"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 16:16"
        },
        "One day as we were going to the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "place of"
          ]
        },
        " prayer, we were met by a slave girl with a spirit of divination,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "16:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "a spirit of Python"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; that is, a spirit of divination named after the mythical serpent slain by Apollo"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " who earned a large income for her masters by fortune-telling. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 16:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This girl"
          ]
        },
        " followed Paul and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the rest of"
          ]
        },
        " us, shouting, “These men are servants of the Most High God, who are proclaiming to you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " way of salvation!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 16:18"
        },
        "She continued this for many days. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Eventually"
          ]
        },
        " Paul grew so aggravated ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " he turned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said to the spirit, “In ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " name of Jesus Christ I command you to come out of her!” And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the spirit"
          ]
        },
        " left her at that very moment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 16:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the girl’s"
          ]
        },
        " owners saw that their hope of making money was gone, they seized Paul and Silas ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " dragged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " before the authorities in the marketplace. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 16:20"
        },
        "They brought them to the magistrates ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “These men are Jews ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " are throwing our city ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "into turmoil"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 16:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "by"
          ]
        },
        " promoting customs that are unlawful for us Romans to adopt ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " practice.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 16:22"
        },
        "The crowd joined in the attack against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Silas"
          ]
        },
        ", and the magistrates ordered that they be stripped ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " beaten with rods. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 16:23"
        },
        "And after striking them with many blows, they threw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " into prison ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ordered the jailer to guard them securely. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 16:24"
        },
        "On receiving ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " order, he placed them in the inner cell and fastened their feet in the stocks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Conversion of the Jailer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 16:25"
        },
        "About midnight Paul and Silas were praying ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " singing hymns to God, and the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "other"
          ]
        },
        " prisoners were listening to them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 16:26"
        },
        "Suddenly a strong earthquake shook the foundations of the prison. At once all the doors flew open and everyone’s chains came loose."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 16:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the jailer woke up and saw the prison doors open, he drew his sword ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was about to kill himself, presuming that the prisoners had escaped. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 16:28"
        },
        "But Paul called out in a loud voice, “Do not harm yourself! We are all here!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 16:29"
        },
        "Calling for lights, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the jailer"
          ]
        },
        " rushed in and fell trembling ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "before"
          ]
        },
        " Paul and Silas. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 16:30"
        },
        "Then he brought them out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " asked, “Sirs, what must I do to be saved?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 16:31"
        },
        "They replied, “Believe in the Lord Jesus and you will be saved, you and your household.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 16:32"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Silas"
          ]
        },
        " spoke the word of the Lord to him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " to everyone in his house. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 16:33"
        },
        "At that hour of the night, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the jailer"
          ]
        },
        " took them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " washed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " wounds. And without delay, he and all his household were baptized. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 16:34"
        },
        "Then he brought them into ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " home and set ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a meal before them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " and all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " household rejoiced that they had come to believe in God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "An Official Apology"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 16:35"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " daylight came, the magistrates sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " officers with the order: “Release those men.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 16:36"
        },
        "The jailer informed Paul: “The magistrates have sent orders to release you. Now you may go on your way in peace.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 16:37"
        },
        "But Paul said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the officers"
          ]
        },
        ", “They beat us publicly without a trial ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " threw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        " into prison, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "even though"
          ]
        },
        " we are Roman citizens. And now do they want to send us away secretly? Absolutely not! Let them come themselves and escort us out!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 16:38"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " the officers relayed this message to the magistrates, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " were alarmed to hear that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Silas"
          ]
        },
        " were Roman citizens. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 16:39"
        },
        "They came to appease them and led them out, requesting that they leave the city. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 16:40"
        },
        "After ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Silas"
          ]
        },
        " came out of the prison, they went to Lydia’s house to see the brothers and encourage ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". Then they left ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the city "
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "17",
      "sid": "ACT 17"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Uproar in Thessalonica"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 17:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they had passed through Amphipolis and Apollonia, they came to Thessalonica, where there was a Jewish synagogue. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 17:2"
        },
        "As was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " custom, Paul went into ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the synagogue"
          ]
        },
        ", and on three Sabbaths he reasoned with them from the Scriptures, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 17:3"
        },
        "explaining and proving that the Christ had to suffer and rise from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead. “This Jesus I am proclaiming to you is the Christ,” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he declared "
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 17:4"
        },
        "Some of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Jews"
          ]
        },
        " were persuaded and joined Paul and Silas, along with a large number of God-fearing Greeks and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "quite"
          ]
        },
        " a few leading women."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 17:5"
        },
        "The Jews, however, became jealous. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they brought in some troublemakers from the marketplace, formed a mob, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sent the city into an uproar. They raided Jason’s house in search of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul and Silas"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "hoping"
          ]
        },
        " to bring them out to the people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 17:6"
        },
        "But when they could not find them, they dragged Jason and some other brothers before the city officials, shouting, “These ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        " who have turned the world ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "upside down"
          ]
        },
        " have now come here, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 17:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " Jason has welcomed them into his home. They ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " all defying Caesar’s decrees, saying that there is another king, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "named "
          ]
        },
        " Jesus!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 17:8"
        },
        "On hearing this, the crowd and city officials were greatly disturbed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 17:9"
        },
        "And they collected bond from Jason and the others ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and then"
          ]
        },
        " released them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Character of the Bereans"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 17:10"
        },
        "As soon as night ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "had fallen"
          ]
        },
        ", the brothers sent Paul and Silas ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "away"
          ]
        },
        " to Berea. On arriving ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ", they went into the Jewish synagogue. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 17:11"
        },
        "Now ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Bereans"
          ]
        },
        " were more noble-minded than the Thessalonians, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " they received the message with great eagerness ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " examined the Scriptures every day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to see"
          ]
        },
        " if these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "teachings"
          ]
        },
        " were true.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "with great eagerness, every day examining the Writings, whether these things were so."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 17:12"
        },
        "As a result, many of them believed, along with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "quite"
          ]
        },
        " a few prominent Greek women and men."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 17:13"
        },
        "But when the Jews from Thessalonica learned that Paul was also proclaiming the word of God in Berea, they went there themselves to incite and agitate the crowds. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 17:14"
        },
        "The brothers immediately sent Paul to the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "coast"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " Silas and Timothy remained ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in Berea"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 17:15"
        },
        "Those who escorted Paul brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to Athens and then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "returned"
          ]
        },
        " with instructions for Silas and Timothy to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "join"
          ]
        },
        " him as soon as possible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul in Athens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 17:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        " Paul was waiting for them in Athens, he was deeply disturbed in his spirit to see that the city was full of idols. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 17:17"
        },
        "So he reasoned in the synagogue with the Jews and God-fearing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Gentiles"
          ]
        },
        ", and in the marketplace with those he met each day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 17:18"
        },
        "Some Epicurean and Stoic philosophers also began to debate with him. Some ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of them"
          ]
        },
        " asked, “What ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " this babbler trying to say?” Others ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "said"
          ]
        },
        ", “He seems to be advocating foreign gods.” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They said this"
          ]
        },
        " because ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " was proclaiming the good news of Jesus and the resurrection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 17:19"
        },
        "So they took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to the Areopagus,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Ares Hill "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Mars Hill"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 22 and added for clarity in verse 33"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " they asked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", “May we know what this new teaching ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " you are presenting? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 17:20"
        },
        "For you are bringing some strange notions to our ears, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " we want to know what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they"
          ]
        },
        " mean.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 17:21"
        },
        "Now all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Athenians and foreigners who lived there spent their time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "doing"
          ]
        },
        " nothing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "more"
          ]
        },
        " than hearing and articulating new ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "ideas"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Address in the Areopagus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 17:22"
        },
        "Then Paul stood up in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " meeting",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in the middle"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " of the Areopagus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " Athens, I see that in every way you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " very religious. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 17:23"
        },
        "For as I walked around and examined your objects of worship, I even found an altar with this inscription:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "pc",
      "content": [
        "TO AN UNKNOWN GOD."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Therefore what you worship as something unknown, I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "now"
          ]
        },
        " proclaim to you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 17:24"
        },
        "The God who made the world and everything in it is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord of heaven and earth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "does"
          ]
        },
        " not live in temples made by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "human"
          ]
        },
        " hands. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 17:25"
        },
        "Nor is He served by human hands, as if He needed anything, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "because"
          ]
        },
        " He Himself gives everyone life and breath and everything ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "else"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 17:26"
        },
        "From one ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:26 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "From one"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "From one blood"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " He made every nation of men, that they should inhabit the whole earth; and He determined ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " appointed times and the boundaries of their lands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 17:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God intended that "
          ]
        },
        " they would seek ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " perhaps reach out for Him and find ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ", though He is not far from each one of us. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 17:28"
        },
        "‘For in Him we live and move and have our being.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "This is probably a quote from the Cretan philosopher Epimenides of Knossos."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " As some of your ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " poets have said, ‘We are ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " offspring.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "This is probably a quote from the poem “Phainomena” by the Cilician philosopher Aratus."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 17:29"
        },
        "Therefore, being offspring of God, we should not think that the Divine Being is like gold or silver or stone, an image formed by man’s skill and imagination."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 17:30"
        },
        "Although God overlooked the ignorance of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "earlier"
          ]
        },
        " times, He now commands all people everywhere to repent. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 17:31"
        },
        "For He has set a day when He will judge the world with justice by the Man He has appointed. He has given proof ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of this"
          ]
        },
        " to everyone by raising Him from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 17:32"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they heard about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " resurrection of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, some began to mock ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "others"
          ]
        },
        " said, “We want to hear you again on this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "topic"
          ]
        },
        ".” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 17:33"
        },
        "At that, Paul left ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Areopagus"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 17:34"
        },
        "But some",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "17:34 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "some men"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " joined him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " believed, including Dionysius the Areopagite, a woman named Damaris, and others ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who were"
          ]
        },
        " with them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "18",
      "sid": "ACT 18"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Ministers in Corinth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1CO 1:1-3",
          "content": [
            "1 Corinthians 1:1–3"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "2CO 1:1-2",
          "content": [
            "2 Corinthians 1:1–2"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 18:1"
        },
        "After this, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " left Athens ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went to Corinth. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 18:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "There"
          ]
        },
        " he found a Jew named Aquila, a native of Pontus, who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "had"
          ]
        },
        " recently come from Italy with his wife Priscilla because Claudius had ordered all the Jews to leave Rome. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " went to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "visit "
          ]
        },
        " them, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 18:3"
        },
        "and he stayed and worked with them because they were tentmakers by trade, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "just as"
          ]
        },
        " he was."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 18:4"
        },
        "Every Sabbath he reasoned in the synagogue, trying to persuade Jews and Greeks alike. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 18:5"
        },
        "And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus is the Christ. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 18:6"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they opposed and insulted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", he shook out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " garments ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " told them, “Your blood ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "be"
          ]
        },
        " on your ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " heads! I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "am"
          ]
        },
        " innocent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of it"
          ]
        },
        ". From now on I will go to the Gentiles.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 18:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " left the synagogue ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went next door to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " house of Titus Justus,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "ECM; SBL, NE, and WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Titius Justus"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Justus"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " a worshiper of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 18:8"
        },
        "Crispus, the synagogue leader, and his whole household believed in the Lord. And many of the Corinthians who heard  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the message "
          ]
        },
        " believed and were baptized."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 18:9"
        },
        "One night the Lord spoke to Paul in a vision: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "Do"
              ]
            },
            " not be afraid; keep on speaking; ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "do"
              ]
            },
            " not be silent. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "10",
              "sid": "ACT 18:10"
            },
            "For I am with you and no one will lay a hand on you, because I have many people in this city.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 18:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " stayed for a year and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a half"
          ]
        },
        ", teaching the word of God among ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Corinthians"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul before Gallio"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 18:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        " Gallio was proconsul of Achaia, the Jews coordinated an attack on Paul and brought him before the judgment seat. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 18:13"
        },
        "“This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        " is persuading the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " to worship God in ways contrary to the law,” they said."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 18:14"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "just as"
          ]
        },
        " Paul was about to speak, Gallio told the Jews, “If this matter involved a wrongdoing or vicious crime, O Jews, it would be reasonable for me to hear your ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "complaint "
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 18:15"
        },
        "But since it is a dispute about words and names and your own law, settle ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " yourselves. I refuse to be a judge of such things.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 18:16"
        },
        "And he drove them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "away"
          ]
        },
        " from the judgment seat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 18:17"
        },
        "At this, the crowd",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "they all"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "all the Greeks"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " seized Sosthenes the synagogue leader ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " beat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " in front of the judgment seat. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " none of this was of concern to Gallio."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Returns to Antioch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 18:18"
        },
        "Paul remained ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in Corinth"
          ]
        },
        " for quite some time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "before"
          ]
        },
        " saying goodbye to the brothers. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He had"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " head shaved in Cenchrea to keep a vow he had ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "made "
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and then"
          ]
        },
        " he sailed for Syria, accompanied by Priscilla and Aquila."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 18:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they reached Ephesus, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " left ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Priscilla and Aquila"
          ]
        },
        ". He himself went into the synagogue ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " reasoned with the Jews. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 18:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they asked ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to stay for a while longer, he declined. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 18:21"
        },
        "But as he left, he said, “I will come back",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "I must by all means keep this feast that comes in Jerusalem, but I will come back"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "if"
          ]
        },
        " God is willing.” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And"
          ]
        },
        " he set sail from Ephesus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 18:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When Paul"
          ]
        },
        " had landed at Caesarea, he went up and greeted the church ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "at Jerusalem "
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:22 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "he went up and greeted the church"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Then"
          ]
        },
        " he went down to Antioch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Third Missionary Journey Begins"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 13:1-3",
          "content": [
            "Acts 13:1–3"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 15:36-41",
          "content": [
            "Acts 15:36–41"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 18:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " had spent some time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in Antioch"
          ]
        },
        ", he traveled from place to place throughout the region of Galatia and Phrygia, strengthening all the disciples."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 18:24"
        },
        "Meanwhile a Jew named Apollos, a native of Alexandria, came to Ephesus. He was an eloquent man, well versed in the Scriptures. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 18:25"
        },
        "He had been instructed in the way of the Lord and was fervent in spirit. He spoke and taught accurately about Jesus,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "18:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "about the Lord"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "though"
          ]
        },
        " he knew only the baptism of John. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 18:26"
        },
        "And he began to speak boldly in the synagogue. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they took him aside and explained to him the way of God more accurately."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 18:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Apollos"
          ]
        },
        " resolved to cross over to Achaia, the brothers encouraged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " wrote to the disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " to welcome him. On his arrival, he ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was a"
          ]
        },
        " great help to those who by grace had believed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 18:28"
        },
        "For he powerfully refuted the Jews in public ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "debate"
          ]
        },
        ", proving from the Scriptures ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus is the Christ."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "19",
      "sid": "ACT 19"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Holy Spirit Received at Ephesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 10:44-48",
          "content": [
            "Acts 10:44–48"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 19:1"
        },
        "While Apollos was at Corinth, Paul passed through the interior",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the highland"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " came to Ephesus. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "There"
          ]
        },
        " he found some disciples ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 19:2"
        },
        "and asked them, “Did you receive ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit when you became believers?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“No,” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they answered"
          ]
        },
        ", “we have not even heard that there is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 19:3"
        },
        "“Into what, then, were you baptized?” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“The baptism of John,” they replied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 19:4"
        },
        "Paul explained: “John’s baptism was a baptism of repentance. He told the people to believe in the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " coming after him, that is, in Jesus.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 19:5"
        },
        "On hearing this, they were baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 19:6"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " Paul laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them, and they spoke in tongues and prophesied. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 19:7"
        },
        "There were about twelve men in all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Ministers in Ephesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EPH 1:1-2",
          "content": [
            "Ephesians 1:1–2"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "REV 2:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Revelation 2:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 19:8"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " went into the synagogue ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " spoke boldly ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " for three months, arguing persuasively about the kingdom of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 19:9"
        },
        "But when some of them stubbornly refused to believe ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " publicly maligned the Way, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " left ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the synagogue"
          ]
        },
        " to conduct daily discussions in the lecture hall of Tyrannus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 19:10"
        },
        "This continued for two years, so that everyone who lived in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in Asia"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey; similarly in verses 22, 26, 27, and 31."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Jews and Greeks alike, heard the word of the Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 19:11"
        },
        "God did extraordinary miracles through the hands of Paul, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 19:12"
        },
        "so that even handkerchiefs",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "soudaria"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and aprons that had touched him were taken to the sick, and the diseases and evil spirits left them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Seven Sons of Sceva"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 19:13"
        },
        "Now ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there were"
          ]
        },
        " some itinerant Jewish exorcists who tried to invoke the name of the Lord Jesus over those with evil spirits. They would say, “I command you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "by"
          ]
        },
        " Jesus, whom Paul proclaims.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 19:14"
        },
        "Seven sons of Sceva, a Jewish chief priest, were doing this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 19:15"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one day"
          ]
        },
        " the evil spirit responded, “Jesus I know, and I know about Paul, but who are you?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 19:16"
        },
        "Then the man with the evil spirit jumped on them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " overpowered them all. The attack was so violent that they ran out of the house naked and wounded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 19:17"
        },
        "This became known to all the Jews and Greeks living in Ephesus, and fear came over all of them. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " the name of the Lord Jesus was held in high honor. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 19:18"
        },
        "Many who had believed now came forward, confessing and disclosing their deeds. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 19:19"
        },
        "And a number of those who had practiced magic arts brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " books ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " burned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in front of everyone. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the value of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the books"
          ]
        },
        " was calculated, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the total came to"
          ]
        },
        " fifty thousand drachmas.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "fifty thousand pieces of silver. "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "A drachma was a silver coin worth about one day’s wages."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 19:20"
        },
        "So the word of the Lord powerfully continued to spread and prevail."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Riot in Ephesus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 19:21"
        },
        "After these things had happened, Paul resolved in the Spirit",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "resolved in spirit"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to go to Jerusalem, passing through Macedonia and Achaia. “After I have been there,” he said, “I must see Rome as well.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 19:22"
        },
        "He sent two of his helpers, Timothy and Erastus, to Macedonia, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "while"
          ]
        },
        " he stayed for a time in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 19:23"
        },
        "About that time there arose a great disturbance",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "there arose no little disturbance"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " about the Way. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 19:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It began with"
          ]
        },
        " a silversmith named Demetrius who made silver shrines of Artemis, bringing much business",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:24 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "bringing no little business"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to the craftsmen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 19:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Demetrius"
          ]
        },
        " assembled ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the craftsmen"
          ]
        },
        ", along with the workmen in related trades. “Men,” he said, “you know that this business is our ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "source of"
          ]
        },
        " prosperity. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 19:26"
        },
        "And you can see and hear that not only in Ephesus, but in nearly the whole ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia, this Paul has persuaded a great number of people to turn away. He says that man-made ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "gods"
          ]
        },
        " are no gods ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "at all"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 19:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "There is"
          ]
        },
        " danger not only ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " our business will fall into disrepute, but also ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " the temple of the great goddess Artemis will be discredited and her majesty deposed — ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "she"
          ]
        },
        " who is worshiped by all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of "
          ]
        },
        " Asia and the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "whole"
          ]
        },
        " world.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 19:28"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the men"
          ]
        },
        " heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they were enraged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began shouting, “Great ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " Artemis of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Ephesians!” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 19:29"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Soon"
          ]
        },
        " the whole city was in disarray. They rushed together into the theatre, dragging with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " Gaius and Aristarchus, Paul’s traveling companions from Macedonia."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 19:30"
        },
        "Paul wanted to go before the assembly, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " the disciples would not allow him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 19:31"
        },
        "Even some of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul’s"
          ]
        },
        " friends who were officials of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "19:31 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "friends who were Asiarchs"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " sent word to him, begging him not to venture into the theatre."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 19:32"
        },
        "Meanwhile the assembly was in turmoil. Some were shouting one thing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and some another"
          ]
        },
        ", and most ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of them"
          ]
        },
        " did not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "even"
          ]
        },
        " know why they were there. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 19:33"
        },
        "The Jews in the crowd pushed Alexander ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "forward"
          ]
        },
        " to explain himself, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " motioned for silence so he could make ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " defense to the people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 19:34"
        },
        "But when they realized that he was a Jew, they all shouted in unison for about two hours: “Great ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " Artemis of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Ephesians!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 19:35"
        },
        "Finally the city clerk quieted the crowd ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " declared, “Men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " Ephesus, doesn’t ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "everyone"
          ]
        },
        " know that the city of Ephesus is guardian of the temple of the great Artemis and of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "her image"
          ]
        },
        ", which fell from heaven? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 19:36"
        },
        "Since these things are undeniable, you ought to be calm and not do anything rash. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 19:37"
        },
        "For you have brought these men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "here"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "though they have"
          ]
        },
        " neither robbed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " temple nor blasphemed our goddess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 19:38"
        },
        "So if Demetrius and his fellow craftsmen have a complaint against anyone, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " courts are open and proconsuls are available. Let them bring charges against one another ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there "
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 19:39"
        },
        "But if you are seeking anything beyond this, it must be settled in a legal assembly. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 19:40"
        },
        "For we are in jeopardy of being charged with rioting for today’s ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "events"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " we have no justification to account for this commotion.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 19:41"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " he had said ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", he dismissed the assembly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "20",
      "sid": "ACT 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul in Macedonia and Greece"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 20:1"
        },
        "When the uproar had ended, Paul sent for the disciples. And after encouraging ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ", he said goodbye ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " left for Macedonia. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 20:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " traveling through that area and speaking many words of encouragement, he arrived in Greece, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 20:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " he stayed three months. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And when"
          ]
        },
        " the Jews formed a plot against him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " he was about to sail for Syria, he decided to go back through Macedonia."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 20:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " was accompanied by Sopater ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "son of"
          ]
        },
        " Pyrrhus from Berea, Aristarchus and Secundus from Thessalonica, Gaius from Derbe, Timothy, and Tychicus and Trophimus from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "from Asia"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey; also in verses 16 and 18."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 20:5"
        },
        "These ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        " went on ahead ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " waited for us in Troas. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 20:6"
        },
        "And after the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Feast"
          ]
        },
        " of Unleavened Bread,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "after the days of the Unleavened"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 12:14-20",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 12:14–20"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " we sailed from Philippi, and five days later we rejoined them in Troas, where we stayed seven days."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Eutychus Revived at Troas"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "2KI 4:18-37",
          "content": [
            "2 Kings 4:18–37"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 20:7"
        },
        "On the first ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " of the week we came together to break bread. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Since"
          ]
        },
        " Paul was ready to leave the next day, he talked to them and kept on speaking until midnight."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 20:8"
        },
        "Now there were many lamps in the upper room where we were gathered. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 20:9"
        },
        "And a certain young man named Eutychus, seated in the window, was sinking into a deep sleep as Paul talked on and on. When he was sound asleep, he fell from the third story and was picked up dead. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 20:10"
        },
        "But Paul went down, threw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "himself"
          ]
        },
        " on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the young man"
          ]
        },
        ", and embraced ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not be alarmed!” he said. “He is still alive!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 20:11"
        },
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " went back upstairs, broke bread, and ate. And after speaking until daybreak, he departed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 20:12"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " greatly relieved to take the boy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "home"
          ]
        },
        " alive."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "From Troas to Miletus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 20:13"
        },
        "We went on ahead to the ship ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sailed to Assos, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " we were to take Paul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "aboard"
          ]
        },
        ". He had arranged this because he was going there on foot. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 20:14"
        },
        "And when he met us at Assos, we took him aboard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went on to Mitylene. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 20:15"
        },
        "Sailing on from there, we arrived the next ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " opposite Chios. The ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " after that we arrived at Samos, and",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and, after remaining at Trogyllium,"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " on the following ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " we came to Miletus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 20:16"
        },
        "Paul had decided to sail past Ephesus to avoid spending time in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia, because he was in a hurry to reach Jerusalem, if possible, by the day of Pentecost.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Harvest"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "(see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 23:16",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 23:16"
                  ]
                },
                ") or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Feast of Weeks"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "(see ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 34:22",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 34:22"
                  ]
                },
                ")."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Farewell to the Ephesians"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 20:17"
        },
        "From Miletus, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " sent to Ephesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " the elders of the church."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 20:18"
        },
        "When they came to him, he said, “You know how I lived the whole time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I was"
          ]
        },
        " with you, from the first day I arrived in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 20:19"
        },
        "I served the Lord with great humility and with tears, especially in the trials that came upon me through the plots of the Jews. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 20:20"
        },
        "I did not shrink back from declaring ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anything"
          ]
        },
        " that was helpful to you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " I taught you publicly and from house to house, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 20:21"
        },
        "testifying to Jews and Greeks alike ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "about"
          ]
        },
        " repentance to God and faith in our Lord Jesus Christ.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "ECM, TR, and Tischendorf; SBL, NE, BYZ, and WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "our Lord Jesus"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 20:22"
        },
        "And now, compelled by the Spirit, I am going to Jerusalem, not knowing what will happen to me ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 20:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I"
          ]
        },
        " only ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "know"
          ]
        },
        " that in town after town the Holy Spirit warns me that chains and afflictions await me. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 20:24"
        },
        "But I consider my life of no value to me, if only I may finish my course and  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "complete "
          ]
        },
        " the ministry I have received from the Lord Jesus — ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the ministry "
          ]
        },
        " of testifying to the good news of God’s grace."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 20:25"
        },
        "Now I know that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "none of"
          ]
        },
        " you among whom I have preached the kingdom will see my face ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "again"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 20:26"
        },
        "Therefore I testify to you this day that I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "am"
          ]
        },
        " innocent of the blood of all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:26 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EZK 33:8-9",
                  "content": [
                    "Ezekiel 33:8–9"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 20:27"
        },
        "For I did not shrink back from declaring to you the whole will of God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 20:28"
        },
        "Keep watch over yourselves and the entire flock of which the Holy Spirit has made you overseers. Be shepherds of the church of God,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Tischendorf "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "of the Lord"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; BYZ and PT "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "of the Lord and God"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " which He purchased with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " own blood.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "20:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "with the blood of His own Son."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 20:29"
        },
        "I know that after my departure, savage wolves will come in among you and will not spare the flock. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 20:30"
        },
        "Even from your own number, men will rise up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " distort ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the truth"
          ]
        },
        " to draw away disciples after them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 20:31"
        },
        "Therefore be alert ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " remember that for three years I never stopped warning each ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of you"
          ]
        },
        " night and day with tears."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 20:32"
        },
        "And now I commit you to God and to the word of His grace, which can build ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        " up and give you an inheritance among all who are sanctified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 20:33"
        },
        "I have not coveted anyone’s silver or gold or clothing. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 20:34"
        },
        "You yourselves know that these hands ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of mine"
          ]
        },
        " have ministered to my ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " needs and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those of"
          ]
        },
        " my companions. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 20:35"
        },
        "In everything, I showed you that by this kind of hard work we must help the weak, remembering the words of the Lord Jesus Himself: ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘It is more blessed to give than to receive.’"
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 20:36"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " had said this, he knelt down with all of them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " prayed. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 20:37"
        },
        "They all wept openly ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " they embraced Paul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " kissed him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 20:38"
        },
        "They were especially grieved by his statement that they would ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "never"
          ]
        },
        " see his face ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "again"
          ]
        },
        ". Then they accompanied him to the ship."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "21",
      "sid": "ACT 21"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Journey to Jerusalem"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 21:1"
        },
        "After we had torn ourselves away from them, we sailed directly to Cos, and the next ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " on to Rhodes, and from there to Patara. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 21:2"
        },
        "Finding a ship crossing over to Phoenicia, we boarded ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " set sail. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 21:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " sighting Cyprus and passing south of it, we sailed on to Syria and landed at Tyre, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " the ship was to unload ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " cargo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 21:4"
        },
        "We sought out the disciples ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in Tyre"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " stayed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with them"
          ]
        },
        " seven days. Through the Spirit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they"
          ]
        },
        " kept telling Paul not to go up to Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 21:5"
        },
        "But when our time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " had ended, we set out on our journey. All ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the disciples"
          ]
        },
        ", with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " wives and children, accompanied us out of the city and knelt down on the beach to pray ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with us"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 21:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And"
          ]
        },
        " after we had said our farewells, we went aboard the ship, and they returned home."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 21:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " we had finished ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " voyage from Tyre, we landed at Ptolemais, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " we greeted the brothers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " stayed with them for a day."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Visits Philip the Evangelist"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 21:8"
        },
        "Leaving the next day, we went on to Caesarea and stayed at the home of Philip the evangelist, who was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " of the Seven.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "21:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ACT 6:5",
                  "content": [
                    "Acts 6:5"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 21:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " had four unmarried daughters who prophesied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 21:10"
        },
        "After we had been there several days, a prophet named Agabus came down from Judea. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 21:11"
        },
        "Coming over to us, he took Paul’s belt, bound his ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " feet and hands, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “The Holy Spirit says: ‘In this way the Jews of Jerusalem will bind the owner of this belt and hand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " over to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Gentiles.’” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 21:12"
        },
        "When we heard this, we and the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " there pleaded with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " not to go up to Jerusalem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 21:13"
        },
        "Then Paul answered, “Why are you weeping and breaking my heart? I am ready not only to be bound, but also to die in Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 21:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " he would not be dissuaded, we quieted down ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “The Lord’s will be done.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 21:15"
        },
        "After these days, we packed up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " went on to Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 21:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Some"
          ]
        },
        " of the disciples from Caesarea accompanied us, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " they took us to stay at the home of Mnason ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Cypriot, an early disciple."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Arrival at Jerusalem"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 21:17"
        },
        "When we arrived in Jerusalem, the brothers welcomed us joyfully. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 21:18"
        },
        "The next ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " Paul went in with us to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "see"
          ]
        },
        " James, and all the elders were present. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 21:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " greeted them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " recounted one by one the things that God had done among the Gentiles through his ministry."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 21:20"
        },
        "When they heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", they glorified God. Then they said to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        ", “You see, brother, how many thousands of Jews have believed, and all of them are zealous for the law. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 21:21"
        },
        "But they are under the impression that you teach all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Jews who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "live"
          ]
        },
        " among the Gentiles to forsake Moses, telling them not to circumcise ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " children ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " observe ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " customs. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 21:22"
        },
        "What then should ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we do"
          ]
        },
        "? They will certainly hear that you have come."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 21:23"
        },
        "Therefore do what we advise you. There are four men with us who have taken a vow. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 21:24"
        },
        "Take these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        ", purify yourself along with them, and pay their expenses so ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "they can have"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " heads shaved. Then everyone will know that there is no truth ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to these"
          ]
        },
        " rumors about you, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " you also live in obedience to the law."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 21:25"
        },
        "As for the Gentile believers, we have written ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to them"
          ]
        },
        " our decision ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " they must abstain from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "food"
          ]
        },
        " sacrificed to idols, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " blood, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " the meat of strangled animals, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " sexual immorality.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 21:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " the next day Paul took the men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " purified himself along with them. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Then"
          ]
        },
        " he entered the temple to give notice of the date ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when their"
          ]
        },
        " purification would be complete ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " the offering would be made for each of them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Seized at the Temple"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 21:27"
        },
        "When the seven days were almost over, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " Jews from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "21:27 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "from Asia"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. "
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " at the temple. They stirred up the whole crowd and seized him, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 21:28"
        },
        "crying out, “Men ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " Israel, help us! This is the man who teaches everyone everywhere against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " people and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "against our"
          ]
        },
        " law and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "against"
          ]
        },
        " this place. Furthermore, he has brought Greeks into the temple and defiled this holy place.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 21:29"
        },
        "For they had previously seen Trophimus the Ephesian with him in the city, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " they assumed that Paul had brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " into the temple."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 21:30"
        },
        "The whole city was stirred up, and the people rushed together. They seized Paul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " dragged him out of the temple, and at once the gates were shut. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 21:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "While"
          ]
        },
        " they were trying to kill him, the commander of the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Roman"
          ]
        },
        " regiment",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "21:31 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the commander of the cohort"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " received a report that all Jerusalem was in turmoil. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 21:32"
        },
        "Immediately he took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " soldiers and centurions ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ran down to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the crowd"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When the people"
          ]
        },
        " saw the commander and the soldiers, they stopped beating Paul."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 21:33"
        },
        "The commander came up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " arrested ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        ", ordering that he be bound with two chains. Then he asked who he was and what he had done."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 21:34"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Some"
          ]
        },
        " in the crowd were shouting one thing, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " another. And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "since"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the commander"
          ]
        },
        " could not get at the truth because of the uproar, he ordered that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " be brought into the barracks. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 21:35"
        },
        "When ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " reached the steps, he had to be carried by the soldiers because of the violence of the mob. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 21:36"
        },
        "For the crowd that followed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " kept shouting, “Away with him!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Addresses the Crowd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 21:37"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        " they were about to take Paul into the barracks, he asked the commander, “May I say something to you?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Do you speak Greek?” ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " replied. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 21:38"
        },
        "“Aren’t you the Egyptian who incited a rebellion some time ago and led four thousand members of the Assassins into the wilderness?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 21:39"
        },
        "But Paul answered, “I am a Jew from Tarsus in Cilicia, a citizen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " no ordinary city. Now I beg you to allow me to speak to the people.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 21:40"
        },
        "Having received permission, Paul stood on the steps ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " motioned to the crowd. A great hush came over ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the crowd"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " he addressed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in Hebrew:",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "21:40 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in Aramaic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in the Hebrew language"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "22",
      "sid": "ACT 22"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Defense to the Crowd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 9:1-19",
          "content": [
            "Acts 9:1–19"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 26:1-23",
          "content": [
            "Acts 26:1–23"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 22:1"
        },
        "“Brothers and fathers, listen now to my defense before you.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 22:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they heard him speak to them in Hebrew,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in Aramaic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in the Hebrew language"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " they became even more quiet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " declared, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 22:3"
        },
        "“I am a Jew, born in Tarsus of Cilicia, but raised in this city. I was educated at the feet of Gamaliel in strict conformity to the law of our fathers. I was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "just as"
          ]
        },
        " zealous for God as any of you are today."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 22:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I"
          ]
        },
        " persecuted this Way even to the death, detaining both men and women and throwing them into prison, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 22:5"
        },
        "as the high priest and the whole Council can testify about me. I even obtained letters from them to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " brothers in Damascus, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " I was on my way to apprehend ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these people"
          ]
        },
        " and bring ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " to Jerusalem to be punished."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 22:6"
        },
        "About noon ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " I was approaching Damascus, suddenly a bright light from heaven flashed around me. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 22:7"
        },
        "I fell to the ground and heard a voice say to me, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 22:8"
        },
        "‘Who are You, Lord?’ I asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘I am Jesus of Nazareth, whom you are persecuting,’"
          ]
        },
        " He replied. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 22:9"
        },
        "My companions saw the light, but they could not understand the voice of the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One"
          ]
        },
        " speaking to me."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 22:10"
        },
        "Then I asked, ‘What should I do, Lord?’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Get up ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "and"
              ]
            },
            " go into Damascus,’"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " told me. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘There you will be told all that you have been appointed to do.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 22:11"
        },
        "Because the brilliance of the light had blinded me, my companions led me by the hand into Damascus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 22:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "There"
          ]
        },
        " a man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "named"
          ]
        },
        " Ananias, a devout observer of the law ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who was"
          ]
        },
        " highly regarded by all the Jews living there, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 22:13"
        },
        "came and stood beside me. ‘Brother Saul,’ he said, ‘receive your sight.’ And at that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "moment"
          ]
        },
        " I could see him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 22:14"
        },
        "Then he said, ‘The God of our fathers has appointed you to know His will and to see the Righteous One and to hear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " voice. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 22:15"
        },
        "You will be His witness to everyone of what you have seen and heard. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 22:16"
        },
        "And now what are you waiting for? Get up, be baptized, and wash your sins ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "away"
          ]
        },
        ", calling on His name.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 22:17"
        },
        "Later, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " I had returned to Jerusalem and was praying at the temple, I fell into a trance ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 22:18"
        },
        "and saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the Lord"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "saw Him"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " saying to me, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Hurry! Leave Jerusalem quickly, because ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the people here"
              ]
            },
            " will not accept your testimony about Me.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 22:19"
        },
        "‘Lord,’ I answered, ‘they know very well that in one synagogue after another I imprisoned and beat those who believed in You. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 22:20"
        },
        "And when the blood of Your witness",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "martyr"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Stephen was shed, I stood there giving my approval and watching over the garments of those who killed him.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 22:21"
        },
        "Then He said to me, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Go! I will send you far away to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " Gentiles.’"
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul the Roman Citizen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 22:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The crowd"
          ]
        },
        " listened to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " until he made this statement. Then they lifted up their voices ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " shouted, “Rid the earth of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        "! He is not fit to live!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 22:23"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        " they were shouting and throwing off ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " cloaks and tossing dust into the air, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 22:24"
        },
        "the commander ordered that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " be brought into the barracks. He directed that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " be flogged and interrogated to determine the reason for this outcry against him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 22:25"
        },
        "But as they stretched him out to strap him down, Paul said to the centurion standing there, “Is it lawful for you to flog a Roman citizen without a trial?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 22:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "On"
          ]
        },
        " hearing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", the centurion went ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " reported ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " to the commander. “What are you going to do?” he said. “This man is a Roman citizen.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 22:27"
        },
        "The commander went to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " and asked, “Tell me, are you a Roman citizen?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Yes,” he answered."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 22:28"
        },
        "“I paid a high price ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for my"
          ]
        },
        " citizenship,” said the commander."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“But I was born a citizen,” Paul replied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 22:29"
        },
        "At once those who were about to interrogate ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " stepped back, and the commander ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "himself"
          ]
        },
        " was alarmed when he realized that he had put a Roman citizen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in chains"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 22:30"
        },
        "The next day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the commander"
          ]
        },
        ", wanting to learn the real reason ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " was accused by the Jews, released him and ordered the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "22:30 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the whole Council"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to assemble. Then he brought Paul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "down"
          ]
        },
        " and had him stand before them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "23",
      "sid": "ACT 23"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul before the Sanhedrin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 23:1"
        },
        "Paul looked directly at the Sanhedrin",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Council"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verses 6, 15, 20, and 28"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Brothers, I have conducted myself before God in all good conscience to this day.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 23:2"
        },
        "At this, the high priest Ananias ordered those standing near ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " to strike him on the mouth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 23:3"
        },
        "Then Paul said to him, “God will strike ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        ", you whitewashed wall! You sit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "here"
          ]
        },
        " to judge me according to the law, yet you yourself violate the law by commanding that I be struck.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 23:4"
        },
        "But those standing nearby said, “How dare you insult the high priest of God!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 23:5"
        },
        "“Brothers,” Paul replied, “I was not aware that he was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " high priest, for it is written: ‘Do not speak evil ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "about the"
          ]
        },
        " ruler of your people.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 22:28",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 22:28"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 23:6"
        },
        "Then Paul, knowing that some of them were Sadducees and the others Pharisees, called out in the Sanhedrin, “Brothers, I am a Pharisee, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " son of a Pharisee. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " because of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my"
          ]
        },
        " hope in the resurrection of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " I am on trial.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 23:7"
        },
        "As soon as he had said ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", a dispute broke out between the Pharisees and Sadducees, and the assembly was divided. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 23:8"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Sadducees say ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " there is neither a resurrection nor angels nor spirits, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Pharisees acknowledge them all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 23:9"
        },
        "A great clamor arose, and some scribes from the party of the Pharisees got up ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " contended sharply, “We find nothing wrong with this man. What if a spirit or an angel has spoken to him?” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 23:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " dispute grew so violent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " the commander was afraid they would tear Paul to pieces. He ordered the soldiers to go down ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " remove him by force and bring ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " into the barracks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 23:11"
        },
        "The following night the Lord stood near ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Take courage! As you have testified about Me in Jerusalem, so also you must testify in Rome.”"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Plot to Kill Paul"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 16:1-4",
          "content": [
            "John 16:1–4"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 23:12"
        },
        "When daylight came, the Jews formed a conspiracy and bound themselves with an oath not to eat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " drink until they had killed Paul. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 23:13"
        },
        "More than forty ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of them"
          ]
        },
        " were involved in this plot. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 23:14"
        },
        "They went to the chief priests and elders ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “We have bound ourselves with a solemn oath ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "not"
          ]
        },
        " to eat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anything"
          ]
        },
        " until we have killed Paul. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 23:15"
        },
        "Now then, you and the Sanhedrin petition the commander to bring him down to you on the pretext of examining his case more carefully. We are ready to kill him on the way.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 23:16"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " the son of Paul’s sister heard about the plot,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the ambush"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " he went into the barracks ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " told Paul. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 23:17"
        },
        "Then Paul called one of the centurions ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Take this young man to the commander; he has something to tell him.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 23:18"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the centurion"
          ]
        },
        " took him to the commander and said, “Paul the prisoner sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " asked me to bring this young man to you. He has something to tell you.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 23:19"
        },
        "The commander took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the young man"
          ]
        },
        " by the hand, drew ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " aside, and asked, “What do you need to tell me?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 23:20"
        },
        "He answered, “The Jews have agreed to ask you to bring Paul to the Sanhedrin tomorrow on the pretext of acquiring more information about him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 23:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " them persuade you, because more than forty men are waiting to ambush him. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They"
          ]
        },
        " have bound themselves with an oath not to eat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " drink until they have killed him; they are ready now, awaiting your consent.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 23:22"
        },
        "So the commander dismissed the young man and instructed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", “Do not tell ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anyone"
          ]
        },
        " that you have reported this to me.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Sent to Felix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 23:23"
        },
        "Then he called two of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " centurions ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Prepare two hundred soldiers, seventy horsemen, and two hundred spearmen to go to Caesarea in the third hour of the night.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "23:23 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, at nine tonight"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 23:24"
        },
        "Provide mounts ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " Paul to take ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " safely to Governor Felix.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 23:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And"
          ]
        },
        " he wrote the following letter:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 23:26"
        },
        "Claudius Lysias,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        "To His Excellency, Governor Felix:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        "Greetings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 23:27"
        },
        "This man was seized by the Jews, and they were about to kill ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " when I came with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my"
          ]
        },
        " troops to rescue ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". For I had learned that he is a Roman citizen, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 23:28"
        },
        "and since I wanted to understand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " charges ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "against"
          ]
        },
        " him, I brought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " down to their Sanhedrin. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 23:29"
        },
        "I found that the accusation involved questions ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "about"
          ]
        },
        " their ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " law, but there was no charge worthy of death or imprisonment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "lf",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 23:30"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " I was informed that there was a plot against the man, I sent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to you at once. I also instructed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " accusers to present ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their case"
          ]
        },
        " against him before you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 23:31"
        },
        "So the soldiers followed their orders ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " brought Paul by night to Antipatris. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 23:32"
        },
        "The next day they returned to the barracks ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " let the horsemen go on with him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 23:33"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When the horsemen"
          ]
        },
        " arrived in Caesarea, they delivered the letter to the governor and presented Paul to him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 23:34"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The governor"
          ]
        },
        " read ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the letter"
          ]
        },
        " and asked what province ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " was from. Learning that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he was"
          ]
        },
        " from Cilicia, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 23:35"
        },
        "he said, “I will hear your case when your accusers arrive.” Then he ordered that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " be kept under guard in Herod’s Praetorium."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "24",
      "sid": "ACT 24"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Tertullus Prosecutes Paul"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 24:1"
        },
        "Five days later the high priest Ananias came down with some elders and a lawyer",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "an orator"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "named"
          ]
        },
        " Tertullus, who presented to the governor ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their case"
          ]
        },
        " against Paul."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 24:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " had been called in, Tertullus opened the prosecution: “Because of you, we have enjoyed a lasting peace, and your foresight has brought improvements to this nation. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 24:3"
        },
        "In every way and everywhere, most excellent Felix, we acknowledge ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " with all gratitude. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 24:4"
        },
        "But in order not to delay you any further, I beg your indulgence to hear us briefly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 24:5"
        },
        "We have found this man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to be"
          ]
        },
        " a pestilence, stirring up dissension among the Jews all over the world. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He is"
          ]
        },
        " a ringleader of the sect of the Nazarenes, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 24:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and he"
          ]
        },
        " even tried to desecrate the temple; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so"
          ]
        },
        " we seized ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "TR includes "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and we would have judged him according to our law. ",
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fv",
                  "content": [
                    "7"
                  ]
                },
                "But Lysias the commander came with great force and took him out of our hands, ",
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fv",
                  "content": [
                    "8"
                  ]
                },
                "ordering his accusers to come before you."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 24:8"
        },
        "By examining him yourself, you will be able to learn ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the truth"
          ]
        },
        " about all our charges ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "against"
          ]
        },
        " him.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 24:9"
        },
        "The Jews concurred, asserting that these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "charges"
          ]
        },
        " were true."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Defense to Felix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 24:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the governor motioned for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " to speak, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " began his response: “Knowing that you have been a judge over this nation for many years, I gladly make my defense. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 24:11"
        },
        "You can verify ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for yourself"
          ]
        },
        " that no more than twelve days ago I went up to Jerusalem to worship. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 24:12"
        },
        "Yet ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my accusers"
          ]
        },
        " did not find me debating with anyone in the temple or riling up a crowd in the synagogues ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " in the city. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 24:13"
        },
        "Nor can they prove to you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "any of"
          ]
        },
        " their charges against me."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 24:14"
        },
        "I do confess to you, however, that I worship the God of our fathers according to the Way, which they call a sect. I believe everything that is laid down by the Law and written in the Prophets, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 24:15"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " I have ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the same"
          ]
        },
        " hope in God that they themselves cherish, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " there will be a resurrection of both ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " righteous and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " wicked. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 24:16"
        },
        "In this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "hope"
          ]
        },
        ", I strive always to maintain a clear conscience before God and man."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 24:17"
        },
        "After several years, then, I returned  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to Jerusalem "
          ]
        },
        " to bring alms to my people and to present offerings. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 24:18"
        },
        "At the time they found me in the temple, I was ceremonially clean ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "inciting"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " crowd ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " an uproar. But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there are"
          ]
        },
        " some Jews from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the province of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "from Asia"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. "
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 24:19"
        },
        "who ought to appear before you and bring charges, if they have anything against me. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 24:20"
        },
        "Otherwise, let ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these men"
          ]
        },
        " state for themselves any crime they found in me when I stood before the Sanhedrin,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "24:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Council"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 24:21"
        },
        "unless ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it was"
          ]
        },
        " this one thing I called out as I stood in their ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "presence"
          ]
        },
        ": ‘",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " concerning ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " resurrection of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " I am on trial before you today.’”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Verdict Postponed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 24:22"
        },
        "Then Felix, who was well informed about the Way, adjourned the hearing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “When Lysias the commander comes, I will decide your case.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 24:23"
        },
        "He ordered the centurion to keep ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " under guard, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " to allow him some freedom and permit his ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "friends"
          ]
        },
        " to minister to his ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "needs"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 24:24"
        },
        "After several days, Felix returned with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " wife Drusilla, who was a Jewess. He sent for Paul and listened to him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "speak"
          ]
        },
        " about faith in Christ Jesus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 24:25"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " expounded on righteousness, self-control, and the coming judgment, Felix became frightened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “You may go for now. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " I find the time, I will call for you.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 24:26"
        },
        "At the same time, he was hoping that Paul would offer him a bribe. So he sent for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " frequently ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " talked with him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 24:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " two years had passed, Felix was succeeded by Porcius Festus. And wishing to do the Jews a favor, Felix left Paul in prison."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "25",
      "sid": "ACT 25"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Trial before Festus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 25:1"
        },
        "Three days after his arrival in the province, Festus went up from Caesarea to Jerusalem, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 25:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "where"
          ]
        },
        " the chief priests and Jewish leaders presented their case against Paul. They urged ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Festus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 25:3"
        },
        "to grant them a concession against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " by summoning him to Jerusalem, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "because "
          ]
        },
        " they were preparing an ambush to kill him along the way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 25:4"
        },
        "But Festus replied, “Paul is being held in Caesarea, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I myself"
          ]
        },
        " am going there soon. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 25:5"
        },
        "So if ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " man has done anything wrong, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "let"
          ]
        },
        " some of your leaders come down with me and accuse him ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 25:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " spending no more than eight or ten days with them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Festus"
          ]
        },
        " went down to Caesarea. The next day he sat on the judgment seat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ordered that Paul be brought in. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 25:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " arrived, the Jews who had come down from Jerusalem stood around him, bringing many serious charges that they could not prove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 25:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Then"
          ]
        },
        " Paul made his defense: “I have committed no offense against the law of the Jews ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " against the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " against Caesar.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 25:9"
        },
        "But Festus, wishing to do the Jews a favor, said to Paul, “Are you willing to go up to Jerusalem to stand trial before me on these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "charges"
          ]
        },
        "?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Appeals to Caesar"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 25:10"
        },
        "Paul replied, “I am standing before the judgment seat of Caesar, where I ought to be tried. I have done nothing wrong to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Jews, as you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "yourself"
          ]
        },
        " know very well. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 25:11"
        },
        "If, however, I am guilty ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " anything worthy of death, I do not refuse to die. But if there is no ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "truth"
          ]
        },
        " to their accusations against me, no one has the right to hand me over to them. I appeal to Caesar!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 25:12"
        },
        "Then Festus conferred with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " council ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " replied, “You have appealed to Caesar. To Caesar you will go!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Festus Consults Agrippa"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 25:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " several days had passed, King Agrippa and Bernice came down to Caesarea to pay their respects to Festus. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 25:14"
        },
        "Since they were staying several days, Festus laid out Paul’s case before the king: “There is a certain man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "whom"
          ]
        },
        " Felix left in prison. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 25:15"
        },
        "While I was in Jerusalem, the chief priests and elders of the Jews presented their case ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " requested a judgment against him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 25:16"
        },
        "I told ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " that it is not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Roman custom to hand a man ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "over"
          ]
        },
        " before ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "he"
          ]
        },
        " has had ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "an"
          ]
        },
        " opportunity to face ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " accusers and defend himself against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " charges."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 25:17"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they came here ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with me"
          ]
        },
        ", I did not delay. The next ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " I sat on the judgment seat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ordered that the man be brought in. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 25:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But when his"
          ]
        },
        " accusers rose to speak, they did not charge ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "any of the"
          ]
        },
        " crimes I had expected. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 25:19"
        },
        "They only had some contentions with him regarding ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " own religion and a certain Jesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " had died, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " whom Paul affirmed to be alive."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 25:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Since"
          ]
        },
        " I was at a loss as to how to investigate these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "matters"
          ]
        },
        ", I asked if he was willing to go to Jerusalem and be tried ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " on these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "charges"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 25:21"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " Paul appealed to be held over for the decision of the Emperor, I ordered that he be held until I could send him to Caesar.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 25:22"
        },
        "Then Agrippa ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "said"
          ]
        },
        " to Festus, “I would like to hear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " man myself.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "“Tomorrow you will hear him,” Festus declared."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul before Agrippa and Bernice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 25:23"
        },
        "The next day Agrippa and Bernice came with great pomp and entered the auditorium, along with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " commanders and leading men of the city. And Festus ordered that Paul be brought in."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 25:24"
        },
        "Then Festus said, “King Agrippa and all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " are present with us, you see this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "man"
          ]
        },
        ". The whole Jewish community has petitioned me about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", both here and in Jerusalem, crying out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " he ought not to live ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "any"
          ]
        },
        " longer. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 25:25"
        },
        "But I found he had done nothing worthy of death, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " since he has now appealed to the Emperor, I decided to send ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 25:26"
        },
        "I have nothing definite to write to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " sovereign about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". Therefore I have brought him before all of you, and especially before you, King Agrippa, so that after this inquiry I may have something to write. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 25:27"
        },
        "For it seems unreasonable to me to send on a prisoner without specifying the charges against him.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "26",
      "sid": "ACT 26"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul’s Testimony to Agrippa"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 9:1-19",
          "content": [
            "Acts 9:1–19"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 22:1-21",
          "content": [
            "Acts 22:1–21"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 26:1"
        },
        "Agrippa said to Paul, “You have permission to speak for yourself.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Then Paul stretched out ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " hand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began his defense: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 26:2"
        },
        "“King Agrippa, I consider myself fortunate to stand before you today to defend myself against all the accusations of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Jews, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 26:3"
        },
        "especially ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "since"
          ]
        },
        " you are acquainted with all the Jewish customs and controversies. I beg ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        ", therefore, to listen to me patiently."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 26:4"
        },
        "Surely all the Jews know how I have lived from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my"
          ]
        },
        " earliest childhood among my own people, and also in Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 26:5"
        },
        "They have known me for a long time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " can testify, if they are willing, that I lived as a Pharisee, adhering to the strictest sect of our religion."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 26:6"
        },
        "And now I stand on trial because of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my"
          ]
        },
        " hope in the promise ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " God made to our fathers, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 26:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the promise "
          ]
        },
        " our twelve tribes are hoping to see fulfilled as they earnestly serve ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God "
          ]
        },
        " day and night. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " because of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " hope, O king, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " I am accused by the Jews. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 26:8"
        },
        "Why ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "would"
          ]
        },
        " any of you consider it incredible that God raises ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 26:9"
        },
        "So then, I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "too"
          ]
        },
        " was convinced that I ought to do all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I could"
          ]
        },
        " to oppose the name of Jesus of Nazareth. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 26:10"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " is what I did in Jerusalem. With authority from the chief priests I put many of the saints in prison, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " they were condemned to death, I cast my vote against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 26:11"
        },
        "I frequently had them punished in the synagogues, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " I tried to make ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " blaspheme. In my raging fury against them, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I"
          ]
        },
        " even ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "went"
          ]
        },
        " to foreign cities to persecute ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 26:12"
        },
        "In this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "pursuit"
          ]
        },
        " I was on my way to Damascus with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " authority and commission of the chief priests. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 26:13"
        },
        "About noon, O king, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as I was"
          ]
        },
        " on the road, I saw a light from heaven, brighter than the sun, shining around me and my companions. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 26:14"
        },
        "We all fell to the ground, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " I heard a voice say to me in Hebrew,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "26:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in Aramaic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in the Hebrew language "
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me? ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "It is"
              ]
            },
            " hard for you to kick against ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " goads.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 26:15"
        },
        "‘Who are You, Lord?’ I asked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "‘I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting,’"
          ]
        },
        " the Lord replied. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            " ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "16",
              "sid": "ACT 26:16"
            },
            "‘But get up and stand on your feet. For I have appeared to you to appoint you as a servant and as a witness of what you have seen from Me and what I will show you. ",
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "17",
              "sid": "ACT 26:17"
            },
            "I will rescue you from ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "your own"
              ]
            },
            " people and from the Gentiles. I am sending you to ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "verse",
              "marker": "v",
              "number": "18",
              "sid": "ACT 26:18"
            },
            "to open their eyes, so that they may turn from darkness to light and from the power of Satan to God, ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "that"
              ]
            },
            " they may receive forgiveness of sins and ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "an"
              ]
            },
            " inheritance among those sanctified by faith in Me.’"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 26:19"
        },
        "So then, King Agrippa, I was not disobedient to the heavenly vision. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 26:20"
        },
        "First to those in Damascus and Jerusalem, then to everyone in the region of Judea, and then to the Gentiles, I declared that they should repent and turn to God, performing deeds worthy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of their"
          ]
        },
        " repentance. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 26:21"
        },
        "For this reason the Jews seized me in the temple ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "courts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "26:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the temple"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " tried to kill ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "me"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 26:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " I have had God’s help to this day, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " I stand ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "here"
          ]
        },
        " to testify to small and great alike. I am saying nothing beyond what the prophets and Moses said would happen: ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 26:23"
        },
        "that the Christ would suffer, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and as the"
          ]
        },
        " first to rise from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, would proclaim light to our people and to the Gentiles.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Festus Interrupts Paul’s Defense"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 26:24"
        },
        "At this stage of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul’s"
          ]
        },
        " defense, Festus exclaimed in a loud voice, “You are insane, Paul! ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Your"
          ]
        },
        " great learning is driving you to madness!”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 26:25"
        },
        "But Paul answered, “I am not insane, most excellent Festus; I am speaking words of truth and sobriety. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 26:26"
        },
        "For the king knows about these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "matters"
          ]
        },
        ", and I can speak freely to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ". I am confident that none of this has escaped his ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "notice"
          ]
        },
        ", because ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " was not done in a corner. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 26:27"
        },
        "King Agrippa, do you believe the prophets? I know you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        ".”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 26:28"
        },
        "Then Agrippa ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "said"
          ]
        },
        " to Paul, “Can you persuade me in such a short ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "time"
          ]
        },
        " to become a Christian?”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 26:29"
        },
        "“Short ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " long,” Paul ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "replied"
          ]
        },
        ", “I wish to God that not only you but all who hear me this day may become what I am, except for these chains.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 26:30"
        },
        "Then the king and the governor rose, along with Bernice and those seated with them. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 26:31"
        },
        "On their way out, they said to one another, “This man has done nothing worthy of death or imprisonment.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 26:32"
        },
        "And Agrippa said to Festus, “This man could have been released if he had not appealed to Caesar.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "27",
      "sid": "ACT 27"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Sails for Rome"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 27:1"
        },
        "When it was decided ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " we would sail for Italy, Paul and some other prisoners were handed over to a centurion named Julius, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who belonged to the"
          ]
        },
        " Imperial",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Augustan"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Regiment. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 27:2"
        },
        "We boarded an Adramyttian ship about to sail for ports along ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the coast of"
          ]
        },
        " Asia,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "sail to the places along Asia"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. "
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " we put out to sea. Aristarchus, a Macedonian from Thessalonica, was with us."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 27:3"
        },
        "The next ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " we landed at Sidon, and Julius treated Paul with consideration, allowing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to visit his friends ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " receive ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " care. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 27:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " putting out from there, we sailed to the lee of Cyprus because the winds were against us. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 27:5"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " we had sailed across the open sea off the coast of Cilicia and Pamphylia, we came to Myra in Lycia. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 27:6"
        },
        "There the centurion found an Alexandrian ship sailing for Italy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " put us on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "board"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 27:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " sailing slowly for many days, we arrived off Cnidus. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " the wind impeded us, we sailed to the lee of Crete, opposite Salmone. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 27:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " we had moved along the coast with difficulty, we came to a place called Fair Havens, near ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " town of Lasea."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 27:9"
        },
        "By now much time had passed, and the voyage had already become dangerous because it was after the Fast.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:9 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "That is, Yom Kippur, the Day of Atonement"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " Paul advised ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 27:10"
        },
        "“Men, I can see that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " voyage will be ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "filled"
          ]
        },
        " with disaster and great loss, not only to ship and cargo, but to our ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " lives as well.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 27:11"
        },
        "But contrary to Paul’s advice, the centurion was persuaded by the pilot and by the owner of the ship. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 27:12"
        },
        "Since the harbor was unsuitable to winter in, the majority decided to sail on, hoping that somehow they could reach Phoenix to winter ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Phoenix was"
          ]
        },
        " a harbor in Crete facing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "both"
          ]
        },
        " southwest and northwest."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Storm at Sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JON 1:4-10",
          "content": [
            "Jonah 1:4–10"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 27:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " a ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "gentle"
          ]
        },
        " south wind began to blow, they thought they had ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " opportunity. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " they weighed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "anchor"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sailed along, hugging ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the coast"
          ]
        },
        " of Crete. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 27:14"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it was"
          ]
        },
        " not long ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "before"
          ]
        },
        " a cyclone called the Northeaster swept down across ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the island"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 27:15"
        },
        "Unable to head into the wind, the ship was caught up. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " we gave way ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " let ourselves be driven along."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 27:16"
        },
        "Passing to the lee of a small island called Cauda,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "NE, BYZ, and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Clauda"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " we barely managed to secure the lifeboat. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 27:17"
        },
        "After hoisting it up, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the crew"
          ]
        },
        " used ropes to undergird the ship. And fearing that they would run aground on the sandbars of Syrtis, they lowered the sea anchor",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the sails"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " were driven along."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 27:18"
        },
        "We were tossed so violently ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " the next ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the men"
          ]
        },
        " began to jettison the cargo. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 27:19"
        },
        "On the third ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        ", they threw the ship’s tackle ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "overboard"
          ]
        },
        " with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " own hands. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 27:20"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " neither sun nor stars appeared for many days and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the great"
          ]
        },
        " storm continued to batter us, we abandoned all hope of being saved."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 27:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the men"
          ]
        },
        " had gone a long time without food, Paul stood up among them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, “Men, you should have followed my advice not to sail from Crete. Then ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you would have averted"
          ]
        },
        " this disaster and loss. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 27:22"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " now I urge you to keep up your courage, because you will not experience ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "any"
          ]
        },
        " loss of life, but only of the ship. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 27:23"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "just last"
          ]
        },
        " night an angel of the God to whom I belong and whom I serve stood beside me ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 27:24"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said, ‘",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not be afraid, Paul; you must stand before Caesar. And look, God has granted you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the lives of"
          ]
        },
        " all who sail with you.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 27:25"
        },
        "So take courage, men, for I believe God that it will happen just as He told me. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 27:26"
        },
        "However, we must run aground on some island.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Shipwreck"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 27:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "On"
          ]
        },
        " the fourteenth night we were still being driven across the Adriatic Sea.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:27 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "The Adriatic Sea referred to an area extending well south of Italy to include the central portion of the Mediterranean Sea."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " About midnight the sailors sensed they were approaching land. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 27:28"
        },
        "They took soundings ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " found that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " twenty fathoms ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "deep"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "20 fathoms "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "is approximately 120 feet or 36.6 meters."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Going a little farther, they took another set of soundings that read fifteen fathoms.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "15 fathoms "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "is approximately 90 feet or 27.4 meters."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "ACT 27:29"
        },
        "Fearing that we would run aground on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " rocks, they dropped four anchors from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " stern ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " prayed for daybreak."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 27:30"
        },
        "Meanwhile, the sailors attempted to escape from the ship. Pretending to lower anchors from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " bow, they let the lifeboat ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "down"
          ]
        },
        " into the sea. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 27:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " Paul said to the centurion and the soldiers, “Unless these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "men"
          ]
        },
        " remain with the ship, you cannot be saved.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "ACT 27:32"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " the soldiers cut the ropes to the lifeboat and set it adrift."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "ACT 27:33"
        },
        "Right up to daybreak, Paul kept urging them all to eat: “Today ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is your"
          ]
        },
        " fourteenth day in constant suspense, without taking any food. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "ACT 27:34"
        },
        "So for your ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " preservation, I urge you to eat something, because not a single hair of your head will be lost.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "ACT 27:35"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " he had said this, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " took bread ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " gave thanks to God in front of them all. Then he broke ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began to eat. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "ACT 27:36"
        },
        "They were all encouraged and took ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " food themselves. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "ACT 27:37"
        },
        "In all, there were 276 ",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "27:37 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "WH "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "76"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " of us on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "board"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "ACT 27:38"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the men"
          ]
        },
        " had eaten their fill, they lightened the ship by throwing the grain into the sea."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "ACT 27:39"
        },
        "When daylight came, they did not recognize the land, but they sighted a bay with a sandy beach, where they decided to run the ship ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "aground"
          ]
        },
        " if they could. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "ACT 27:40"
        },
        "Cutting away the anchors, they left ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in the sea as they loosened the ropes ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that held"
          ]
        },
        " the rudders. Then they hoisted the foresail to the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "wind"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " made for the beach. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "41",
          "sid": "ACT 27:41"
        },
        "But the ship struck a sandbar ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ran aground. The bow stuck fast ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " would not move, and the stern was being broken up by the pounding of the waves."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "42",
          "sid": "ACT 27:42"
        },
        "The soldiers planned to kill the prisoners so none of them could swim to freedom. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "43",
          "sid": "ACT 27:43"
        },
        "But the centurion, wanting to spare Paul’s  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "life "
          ]
        },
        ", thwarted their plan. He commanded those who could swim to jump overboard first ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " get to land. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "44",
          "sid": "ACT 27:44"
        },
        "The rest ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were to follow"
          ]
        },
        " on planks and various parts of the ship. In this way everyone was brought safely to land."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "28",
      "sid": "ACT 28"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Ashore on Malta"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "ACT 28:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Once"
          ]
        },
        " we were safely ashore, we learned that the island was called Malta. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "ACT 28:2"
        },
        "The islanders showed us extraordinary kindness. They kindled a fire ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " welcomed all of us because ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it was"
          ]
        },
        " raining and cold."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "ACT 28:3"
        },
        "Paul gathered a bundle of sticks, and as he laid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " on the fire, a viper, driven out by the heat, fastened ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "itself"
          ]
        },
        " to his hand. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "ACT 28:4"
        },
        "When the islanders saw the creature hanging from his hand, they said to one another, “Surely this man is a murderer. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Although he"
          ]
        },
        " was saved from the sea, Justice",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Dike"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; that is, the Greek goddess of justice"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "has"
          ]
        },
        " not allowed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " to live.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "ACT 28:5"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " shook the creature ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "off"
          ]
        },
        " into the fire ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " suffered no ill effects. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "ACT 28:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The islanders"
          ]
        },
        " were expecting him to swell up or suddenly drop dead. But after waiting a long time and seeing nothing unusual happen to him, they changed their minds ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said he was a god."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "ACT 28:7"
        },
        "Nearby stood an estate belonging to Publius, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " chief official of the island. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " welcomed us ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " entertained ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        " hospitably ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " three days. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "ACT 28:8"
        },
        "The father of Publius was sick in bed, suffering from fever and dysentery. Paul went in to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "see"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        ", and after praying ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " placing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " hands on him, he healed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the man"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "ACT 28:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " this had happened, the rest of the sick on the island came and were cured as well."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "ACT 28:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The islanders"
          ]
        },
        " honored us in many ways and supplied ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " needs ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when we were ready"
          ]
        },
        " to sail."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Arrives in Italy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "ACT 28:11"
        },
        "After three months we set sail in an Alexandrian ship that had wintered in the island. It had the Twin Brothers",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Dioscuri"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; that is, the Greek gods Castor and Pollux"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " as a figurehead. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "ACT 28:12"
        },
        "Putting in at Syracuse, we stayed there three days. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "ACT 28:13"
        },
        "From ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "there"
          ]
        },
        " we weighed anchor and came to Rhegium. After one day, a south wind came up, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " on the second day we arrived at Puteoli. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "ACT 28:14"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "There"
          ]
        },
        " we found ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "some"
          ]
        },
        " brothers who invited us to spend ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " week with them. And so we came to Rome."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "ACT 28:15"
        },
        "The brothers there had heard about us ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " traveled as far as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Forum of Appius",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "The Forum of Appius was about 43 miles or 70 kilometers from Rome."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Three Taverns",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "The Three Taverns was about 35 miles or 57 kilometers from Rome."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to meet us. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " Paul saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ", he was encouraged and gave thanks to God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Paul Preaches at Rome"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ISA 6:1-13",
          "content": [
            "Isaiah 6:1–13"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "ACT 28:16"
        },
        "When we arrived in Rome,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the centurion delivered up the prisoners to the captain of the barrack, but"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " Paul was permitted to stay by himself, with a soldier to guard him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "ACT 28:17"
        },
        "After three days, he called together the leaders of the Jews. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " they had gathered, he said to them, “Brothers, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "although"
          ]
        },
        " I have done nothing against ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " people or the customs of our fathers, I was taken prisoner in Jerusalem ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " handed over to the Romans. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "ACT 28:18"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They"
          ]
        },
        " examined me ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " wanted to release ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "me"
          ]
        },
        ", because there was no basis for a death sentence against me. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "ACT 28:19"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " the Jews objected, I was compelled to appeal to Caesar, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "even though"
          ]
        },
        " I have no ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "charge"
          ]
        },
        " to bring against my nation. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "ACT 28:20"
        },
        "So for this reason I have called to see you and speak with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " because of the hope of Israel ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " I am bound with this chain.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "ACT 28:21"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The leaders"
          ]
        },
        " replied, “We have not received ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "any"
          ]
        },
        " letters about you from Judea, nor ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "have"
          ]
        },
        " any of the brothers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from there"
          ]
        },
        " reported or even mentioned anything bad about you. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "ACT 28:22"
        },
        "But we consider your views ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "worth"
          ]
        },
        " hearing, because we know that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " everywhere are speaking against this sect.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "ACT 28:23"
        },
        "So they set a day to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "meet with Paul"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " came to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the place"
          ]
        },
        " he was staying. He expounded to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " from morning to evening, testifying about the kingdom of God and persuading them about Jesus from the Law of Moses and the Prophets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "ACT 28:24"
        },
        "Some ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of them"
          ]
        },
        " were convinced by what he said, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "others"
          ]
        },
        " refused to believe. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "ACT 28:25"
        },
        "They disagreed among ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "themselves"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " began to leave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "after"
          ]
        },
        " Paul had made ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this final"
          ]
        },
        " statement: “The Holy Spirit was right when He spoke to your fathers through Isaiah the prophet:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "ACT 28:26"
        },
        "‘Go to this people and say,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "“You will be ever hearing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " never understanding;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "you will be ever seeing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " never perceiving.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "ACT 28:27"
        },
        "For this people’s heart has grown callous;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "they hardly hear with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " ears,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and they have closed their eyes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "Otherwise they might see with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " eyes,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "hear with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " ears,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "understand with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " hearts,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "and turn, and I would heal them.’",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:27 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 6:9-10",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 6:9–10"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "ACT 28:28"
        },
        "Be advised, therefore, that God’s salvation has been sent to the Gentiles, and they will listen!”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "28:28 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fv",
                  "content": [
                    "29"
                  ]
                },
                "When he had said this, the Jews went away, disputing sharply among themselves."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "ACT 28:30"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Paul"
          ]
        },
        " stayed there two full years in his own rented house, welcoming all who came to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "visit"
          ]
        },
        " him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "ACT 28:31"
        },
        "Boldly ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " freely he proclaimed the kingdom of God and taught about the Lord Jesus Christ."
      ]
    }
  ]
}